WEBVTT

1
00:00:37,208 --> 00:00:38,625
[radio static]

2
00:00:38,708 --> 00:00:40,583
[man 1] <i>I'm a Spurs fan, he's…</i>

3
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:43,833
[overlapping chatter]

4
00:00:43,916 --> 00:00:46,000
[woman 1] <i>I've got a date</i>
<i>with a new guy next week.</i>

5
00:00:47,791 --> 00:00:49,500
[man 2] <i>I think we need some</i>
<i>proper leadership</i>

6
00:00:49,583 --> 00:00:50,666
<i>for young people.</i>

7
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:52,833
[man 3] <i>Who would you ideally</i>
<i>replace him with?</i>

8
00:00:52,916 --> 00:00:55,333
[overlapping chatter continues]

9
00:00:56,458 --> 00:00:58,208
[woman 2] <i>I don't have any unclaimed…</i>

10
00:00:59,083 --> 00:01:01,291
[man 4] <i>…getting youthful…</i>

11
00:01:01,375 --> 00:01:03,166
[man 5] <i>…a black hatchback…</i>

12
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:05,000
[overlapping chatter continues]

13
00:01:05,083 --> 00:01:06,291
[man 6] <i>I need my money,</i>
<i>I've got a mortgage,</i>

14
00:01:06,375 --> 00:01:07,833
<i>I've got bills to pay…</i>

15
00:01:07,916 --> 00:01:08,916
[man 7] <i>…every WhatsApp group.</i>

16
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:10,416
[woman 3] <i>Why don't I meet you</i>
<i>at the car park?</i>

17
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:12,500
[man 8] …<i>learn to pirouette</i>
<i>like a prima ballerina.</i>

18
00:01:12,583 --> 00:01:14,333
…tell her one more
time where our printer is.

19
00:01:14,416 --> 00:01:15,416
It doesn't move.

20
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:17,166
[overlapping chatter continues]

21
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:18,958
You wouldn't have
to replay the whole fight

22
00:01:19,041 --> 00:01:20,708
if you'd just listened to me
in the first place.

23
00:01:22,166 --> 00:01:23,708
[man 9] <i>These supplements make me feel</i>

24
00:01:23,791 --> 00:01:25,125
<i>like more of a man than ever.</i>

25
00:01:25,208 --> 00:01:28,041
The manager's been watching us
on cameras from his office.

26
00:01:29,083 --> 00:01:30,875
[man 10] <i>Don't you think</i>
<i>a lie like that is dangerous?</i>

27
00:01:30,958 --> 00:01:33,291
[overlapping chatter continues]

28
00:01:35,375 --> 00:01:36,791
[man 11] <i>Listen.</i>

29
00:01:36,875 --> 00:01:38,833
<i>This is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.</i>

30
00:01:38,916 --> 00:01:40,791
[overlapping chatter continues]

31
00:01:40,875 --> 00:01:42,708
If anyone finds out about this,

32
00:01:42,791 --> 00:01:44,291
we're both dead, that's it.

33
00:01:44,833 --> 00:01:47,000
[woman 4] <i>I'll be there in three hours.</i>

34
00:01:47,083 --> 00:01:48,583
[notifications chime]

35
00:01:48,666 --> 00:01:50,458
[woman 5] <i>When the King of Glory comes…</i>

36
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:55,791
[overlapping chatter crescendos]

37
00:02:00,208 --> 00:02:01,958
-[chatter stops]
-["Paradise" playing]

38
00:02:02,041 --> 00:02:03,500
[child playing xylophone]

39
00:02:03,583 --> 00:02:05,166
[woman] You're getting good at that.

40
00:02:06,708 --> 00:02:08,666
I've got a very big day in court today

41
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:10,375
and I'm a little nervous.

42
00:02:10,458 --> 00:02:12,958
[boy] I've got football
and I hate football.

43
00:02:13,041 --> 00:02:14,958
[woman laughs]

44
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:20,500
[woman] Come on, get yourself ready.

45
00:02:20,583 --> 00:02:22,458
[boy] I've been ready for ages.

46
00:02:22,541 --> 00:02:23,583
[woman] Oh, yeah?

47
00:02:25,166 --> 00:02:26,750
Have you changed your insulin pod?

48
00:02:27,583 --> 00:02:29,666
-Yep.
-How are your numbers?

49
00:02:31,166 --> 00:02:32,833
-[mobile phone chimes]
-[boy] Ninety-six.

50
00:02:32,916 --> 00:02:34,125
All good.

51
00:02:35,958 --> 00:02:37,833
[man]
<i>♪ But this time it's real ♪</i>

52
00:02:37,916 --> 00:02:39,250
<i>♪ It's something that I feel ♪</i>

53
00:02:39,333 --> 00:02:41,166
<i>♪ If it feels like paradise ♪</i>

54
00:02:41,250 --> 00:02:43,125
<i>♪ Running through</i>
<i>Your bloody veins ♪</i>

55
00:02:43,208 --> 00:02:45,458
<i>♪ You know it's love</i>
<i>Heading your way ♪</i>

56
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:48,208
<i>♪ If it feels like paradise ♪</i>

57
00:02:48,291 --> 00:02:50,041
<i>♪ Running through</i>
<i>Your bloody veins ♪</i>

58
00:02:50,125 --> 00:02:52,916
<i>♪ You know it's love</i>
<i>Heading your way ♪</i>

59
00:02:56,666 --> 00:02:58,416
<i>-♪ My time ♪</i>
-[chorus] <i>♪ My time ♪</i>

60
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:00,083
<i>♪ My t-t-t-t-time ♪</i>

61
00:03:00,166 --> 00:03:02,041
<i>♪ Well, it's a never-ending</i>
<i>Helter-skelter… ♪</i>

62
00:03:02,125 --> 00:03:04,500
One, two, and…

63
00:03:06,041 --> 00:03:07,041
three.

64
00:03:07,125 --> 00:03:08,750
<i>♪ My boom-boom heart ♪</i>

65
00:03:08,833 --> 00:03:10,166
<i>♪ It's a beating</i>
<i>It's a thumping ♪</i>

66
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:11,750
Let's go.

67
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,666
<i>-♪ I know you heard it… ♪</i>
-[song ends]

68
00:03:15,708 --> 00:03:17,458
[boy] We did this fundraising thing

69
00:03:17,541 --> 00:03:19,583
where we got to throw
wet sponges at Mr Pearson.

70
00:03:19,666 --> 00:03:20,916
-[woman] Really?
-Yeah.

71
00:03:25,708 --> 00:03:27,375
[woman chuffs]

72
00:03:27,458 --> 00:03:29,625
-[woman 2] See you later!
-[chuckles]

73
00:03:29,708 --> 00:03:32,666
[woman] What about going in
on your own today, hmm?

74
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:34,208
Mmm-mmm.

75
00:03:34,291 --> 00:03:35,791
Come on, just give it a go.

76
00:03:36,541 --> 00:03:37,541
Hmm?

77
00:03:38,166 --> 00:03:40,500
But I like it when you walk me in.

78
00:03:40,583 --> 00:03:41,958
[chuckles] I know

79
00:03:42,041 --> 00:03:43,541
but it's good to try new things.

80
00:03:44,250 --> 00:03:46,916
Remember when you were afraid
to go ice skating?

81
00:03:49,708 --> 00:03:51,458
I think you'd be the one to miss it.

82
00:03:52,666 --> 00:03:54,083
-[boy grunts]
-Whoa.

83
00:03:55,291 --> 00:03:56,583
I love you.

84
00:03:58,541 --> 00:04:00,458
[kisses] I'm proud of you.

85
00:04:01,125 --> 00:04:03,500
And don't forget to check
your glucose numbers.

86
00:04:04,833 --> 00:04:06,166
I love you, monkey.

87
00:04:06,250 --> 00:04:07,791
-Love you, Mum.
-[woman blows kisses]

88
00:04:13,416 --> 00:04:15,625
[mobile phone ringing]

89
00:04:15,708 --> 00:04:16,875
[automated voice] <i>Ted McBain calling.</i>

90
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,583
[earphone beeps]

91
00:04:20,666 --> 00:04:22,250
-Hi, Ted.
-[Ted] <i>Morning.</i>

92
00:04:23,291 --> 00:04:24,958
<i>They've moved the witness pick-up time.</i>

93
00:04:25,666 --> 00:04:27,333
<i>It's now 10:15.</i>

94
00:04:27,416 --> 00:04:29,291
Okay, got it.

95
00:04:29,375 --> 00:04:31,375
[Ted] <i>Does that leave you</i>
<i>enough time to run in?</i>

96
00:04:31,458 --> 00:04:32,958
Yeah, no problem.

97
00:04:33,875 --> 00:04:35,250
[Ted sighs]

98
00:04:35,333 --> 00:04:36,833
<i>Can we talk about last night?</i>

99
00:04:37,583 --> 00:04:39,541
<i>I thought you were having</i>
<i>a good time and then--</i>

100
00:04:39,625 --> 00:04:41,875
[sighs] You said all you needed to say.

101
00:04:41,958 --> 00:04:44,500
You don't wanna have kids. I have Noah.

102
00:04:44,583 --> 00:04:45,666
And that's that.

103
00:04:46,416 --> 00:04:48,416
[sighs] <i>I said I needed to think about--</i>

104
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:50,666
Look, I understand your position.

105
00:04:50,750 --> 00:04:53,125
Really, if I didn't have Noah,
I'm not sure

106
00:04:53,208 --> 00:04:55,541
if I would get involved with
someone who has a child.

107
00:04:55,625 --> 00:04:56,708
It's okay.

108
00:04:56,791 --> 00:04:58,000
[Ted] <i>You're trying to argue my point</i>

109
00:04:58,083 --> 00:05:00,833
<i>-but it's not even my point.</i>
-Ted, I gotta run.

110
00:05:00,916 --> 00:05:02,250
I'll see you at the office.

111
00:05:03,083 --> 00:05:04,750
<i>-</i>[Ted] <i>Maia--</i>
-[call ends]

112
00:05:06,041 --> 00:05:07,500
[exhales]

113
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
["Heart of Glass" playing]

114
00:05:24,750 --> 00:05:27,458
[woman] <i>♪ Once I had a love</i>
<i>And it was a gas ♪</i>

115
00:05:29,041 --> 00:05:31,500
<i>♪ Soon turned out</i>
<i>Had a heart of glass ♪</i>

116
00:05:33,375 --> 00:05:37,458
<i>♪ Seemed like the real thing</i>
<i>Only to find ♪</i>

117
00:05:37,541 --> 00:05:39,958
<i>♪ Mucho mistrust</i>
<i>Love's gone behind ♪</i>

118
00:05:41,458 --> 00:05:43,291
{\an8}-[song stops]
-[mobile phone ringing]

119
00:05:43,375 --> 00:05:45,958
{\an8}[automated voice] <i>Flora Gibson calling.</i>

120
00:05:46,041 --> 00:05:47,625
{\an8}-[earphone beeps]
-Maia Marten.

121
00:05:47,708 --> 00:05:48,708
[Flora] <i>Maia, the police are here.</i>

122
00:05:48,791 --> 00:05:50,083
<i>You said they wouldn't take my devices.</i>

123
00:05:50,166 --> 00:05:51,250
<i>They've got my computer--</i>

124
00:05:51,333 --> 00:05:52,833
-Flora, stop.
<i>-I don't know what to do!</i>

125
00:05:52,916 --> 00:05:54,916
-Take a breath.
-[Flora breathes deeply]

126
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,541
Good.

127
00:05:56,625 --> 00:05:59,791
Never talk to the police without me, okay?

128
00:06:00,583 --> 00:06:01,958
[Flora] <i>Okay.</i>

129
00:06:02,041 --> 00:06:03,958
Your husband is just trying to scare you.

130
00:06:04,041 --> 00:06:06,041
[Flora] <i>Well, I'm the one</i>
<i>telling the truth, Maia!</i>

131
00:06:06,125 --> 00:06:07,875
<i>He's the criminal.</i>

132
00:06:07,958 --> 00:06:09,208
[Maia] Listen to me.

133
00:06:09,291 --> 00:06:13,250
99% of defending yourself
is telling the right story.

134
00:06:13,916 --> 00:06:15,958
Controlling the narrative.

135
00:06:16,041 --> 00:06:18,166
[Flora] <i>So what's the other 1%?</i>

136
00:06:18,250 --> 00:06:20,208
[exhales] Being innocent.

137
00:06:22,083 --> 00:06:23,958
Listen, Flora, I gotta run.

138
00:06:24,041 --> 00:06:26,958
