171
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:55,458
and you're pulling a prank.

172
00:07:55,541 --> 00:07:57,416
[caller] <i>Then why are you</i>
<i>walking towards the temple?</i>

173
00:07:57,500 --> 00:07:58,791
[breathing heavily]

174
00:08:01,750 --> 00:08:04,291
-[gasps]
-[speaks indistinctly]

175
00:08:04,375 --> 00:08:05,625
[caller] <i>If you don't believe me,</i>

176
00:08:05,708 --> 00:08:07,125
<i>Noah can tell you himself.</i>

177
00:08:07,208 --> 00:08:09,000
<i>Noah, say hi to Mummy.</i>

178
00:08:09,083 --> 00:08:10,541
[Noah] <i>Mum, he's got me</i>
<i>chocolate chip ice cream.</i>

179
00:08:10,625 --> 00:08:12,208
<i>-I love it.</i>
-Noah, where are you?

180
00:08:12,291 --> 00:08:13,958
[Noah] <i>At the temple. Are you here?</i>

181
00:08:14,041 --> 00:08:16,166
Stay exactly where you are. Don't move.

182
00:08:16,250 --> 00:08:17,250
[Noah] <i>I've got to go now.</i>

183
00:08:17,333 --> 00:08:18,458
<i>Your friend said we'll see you later.</i>

184
00:08:18,541 --> 00:08:19,875
No, Noah, you need to get away from him.

185
00:08:19,958 --> 00:08:22,208
-[line disconnects]
-["Heart of Glass" resumes]

186
00:08:23,625 --> 00:08:25,375
[switches music off]

187
00:08:25,458 --> 00:08:27,000
[tense music playing]

188
00:08:27,791 --> 00:08:29,125
[panting]

189
00:08:37,791 --> 00:08:39,833
[distant siren blares]

190
00:08:47,333 --> 00:08:49,333
[Maia grunts]

191
00:08:49,416 --> 00:08:51,750
-My God! Why'd she do that?
-[woman] So rude.

192
00:09:05,583 --> 00:09:07,125
[breathing heavily]

193
00:09:11,583 --> 00:09:13,125
[woman] Hey, get off him!

194
00:09:13,208 --> 00:09:14,500
-What are you doing?
-Sorry.

195
00:09:14,583 --> 00:09:15,833
Are you all right, darling?

196
00:09:16,583 --> 00:09:18,041
[mobile phone chimes]

197
00:09:26,083 --> 00:09:28,458
[man] Yeah, it's like a bush or something.

198
00:09:30,208 --> 00:09:31,208
Ah, here you are.

199
00:09:31,291 --> 00:09:33,250
[woman] So sorry I'm late.
I couldn't find you.

200
00:09:33,333 --> 00:09:34,708
[man] Don't worry about it.

201
00:09:36,041 --> 00:09:37,666
Noah?

202
00:09:39,041 --> 00:09:40,500
Noah?

203
00:09:41,375 --> 00:09:42,666
Noah?

204
00:09:43,458 --> 00:09:45,333
-[tense music continues]
-[woman] Is she okay?

205
00:09:56,833 --> 00:09:58,500
[echoes] Noah?

206
00:10:00,375 --> 00:10:02,375
{\an8}[mobile phone ringing]

207
00:10:02,458 --> 00:10:03,458
{\an8}Where are you?

208
00:10:03,541 --> 00:10:06,625
{\an8}[scam caller] <i>Miss Marten,</i>
<i>you have won £100,000.</i>

209
00:10:06,708 --> 00:10:08,583
{\an8}[ends call]

210
00:10:08,666 --> 00:10:10,166
{\an8}[mobile phone ringing]

211
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:11,416
{\an8}Are you here?

212
00:10:12,625 --> 00:10:14,083
{\an8}Hello?

213
00:10:14,166 --> 00:10:15,375
[caller] <i>Hello.</i>

214
00:10:16,583 --> 00:10:19,416
Now, you listen to me. This game is over.

215
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:20,750
Where are you?

216
00:10:20,833 --> 00:10:22,708
<i>Maia, take a breath.</i>

217
00:10:22,791 --> 00:10:24,083
If you lay a finger on him,

218
00:10:24,166 --> 00:10:26,250
I swear to God I'm gonna kill you.

219
00:10:26,333 --> 00:10:28,833
<i>If we're gonna do this,</i>
<i>you need to calm down.</i>

220
00:10:28,916 --> 00:10:31,083
How dare you tell me to calm down?

221
00:10:32,916 --> 00:10:34,708
[breathing heavily]

222
00:10:35,583 --> 00:10:37,583
Were you a defendant in one of my cases?

223
00:10:38,166 --> 00:10:40,333
-If you were--
<i>-You have a logical mind.</i>

224
00:10:40,416 --> 00:10:43,250
<i>But sometimes logic isn't enough.</i>

225
00:10:43,333 --> 00:10:45,333
[indistinct police radio chatter]

226
00:10:52,375 --> 00:10:54,500
<i>Never talk to the police.</i>

227
00:10:55,375 --> 00:10:57,083
<i>Isn't that what you told Flora?</i>

228
00:11:03,333 --> 00:11:05,000
<i>This is a very simple game.</i>

229
00:11:05,541 --> 00:11:07,125
<i>It's like snakes and ladders.</i>

230
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,125
<i>You follow my rules</i>

231
00:11:09,208 --> 00:11:11,041
<i>and Noah lives.</i>

232
00:11:11,125 --> 00:11:13,125
<i>Disobey, he dies.</i>

233
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,375
[breathing heavily]

234
00:11:17,458 --> 00:11:20,541
<i>Rule number one,</i>
<i>you talk to nobody but me,</i>

235
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:23,708
<i>on the phone, on the street.</i>

236
00:11:24,708 --> 00:11:26,000
<i>Nobody. Understood?</i>

237
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:30,333
<i>-Understood?</i>
-Yes. Yes, I understand.

238
00:11:30,416 --> 00:11:33,583
<i>The second rule, you do</i>
<i>what I say when I say.</i>

239
00:11:34,333 --> 00:11:35,666
<i>You do not bore me.</i>

240
00:11:35,750 --> 00:11:38,416
["The Entertainer" playing]

241
00:11:40,250 --> 00:11:43,125
["The Entertainer" continues playing]

242
00:11:47,083 --> 00:11:48,791
[Maia] <i>Are you still in the park?</i>

243
00:11:48,875 --> 00:11:50,833
[caller] No, we're almost home.

244
00:11:50,916 --> 00:11:52,875
<i>Aren't we, Noah?</i>

245
00:11:53,875 --> 00:11:55,791
<i>So let's begin.</i>

246
00:11:55,875 --> 00:11:57,708
<i>Do you know the men's swimming pond?</i>

247
00:11:57,791 --> 00:11:58,875
Yes.

248
00:11:58,958 --> 00:12:00,125
<i>Run to it.</i>

249
00:12:00,208 --> 00:12:02,208
[tense music playing]

250
00:12:09,041 --> 00:12:11,083
[indistinct chatter]

251
00:12:15,875 --> 00:12:17,875
<i>Now look in the red bin.</i>

252
00:12:18,750 --> 00:12:20,291
[tense music playing]

253
00:12:31,791 --> 00:12:33,041
[music stops]

254
00:12:37,875 --> 00:12:39,250
<i>Do you have it?</i>

255
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,666
<i>There's a package inside.</i>

256
00:12:48,333 --> 00:12:50,291
[Maia breathing heavily]

257
00:13:08,791 --> 00:13:10,916
<i>Your star witness,</i>

258
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,458
<i>Mr Radian Tafa,</i>

259
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:15,791
<i>is under heavy protection</i>
<i>at the Excelsus Hotel.</i>

260
00:13:15,875 --> 00:13:17,791
<i>Today is trial day.</i>

261
00:13:17,875 --> 00:13:21,458
<i>At 10:15, he's gonna be</i>
<i>transported to the Old Bailey</i>

262
00:13:21,541 --> 00:13:24,500
<i>to stand witness against my employer.</i>

263
00:13:24,583 --> 00:13:26,250
<i>But that won't happen</i>

264
00:13:26,333 --> 00:13:28,750
<i>because you're gonna kill him first.</i>

265
00:13:32,375 --> 00:13:33,916
You're too late.

266
00:13:34,791 --> 00:13:37,625
They moved him last night.
He's not even there.

267
00:13:37,708 --> 00:13:41,583
<i>I've heard so many grand</i>
<i>things about Maia Marten</i>

268
00:13:41,666 --> 00:13:43,583
<i>and her ability to spin her own reality</i>

269
00:13:43,666 --> 00:13:45,041
<i>in the courtroom.</i>

270
00:13:46,333 --> 00:13:49,541
<i>But here you are</i>
<i>telling little butterfly lies.</i>

271
00:13:50,875 --> 00:13:52,625
<i>I know you're one of six people</i>

272
00:13:52,708 --> 00:13:54,750
<i>with access to Tafa today,</i>

273
00:13:54,833 --> 00:13:56,666
<i>because you wrote it in an email.</i>

274
00:13:58,041 --> 00:13:59,833
[swimmer laughing]

275
00:14:00,625 --> 00:14:03,166
If you're one of Boyd's men,
I can get you immunity.

276
00:14:03,250 --> 00:14:05,375
You can testify, we can fix everything.

277
00:14:05,458 --> 00:14:06,958
<i>Maia.</i>

278
00:14:07,041 --> 00:14:09,416
<i>I'm a freelancer, a specialist.</i>

279
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:11,041
Okay, whatever he's paying you,

280
00:14:11,125 --> 00:14:12,166
I'll double it.

281
00:14:12,250 --> 00:14:14,166
<i>I've seen your bank balance.</i>
<i>You can't afford me.</i>

282
00:14:14,250 --> 00:14:16,208
I can get you the money, trust me.

283
00:14:16,291 --> 00:14:17,875
<i>Don't bore me!</i>

284
00:14:17,958 --> 00:14:19,416
But why me?

285
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:21,166
<i>Oh, you know why, Maia.</i>

286
00:14:23,166 --> 00:14:25,666
[unsettling musical sting]

287
00:14:25,750 --> 00:14:27,291
I can't kill someone.

288
00:14:27,375 --> 00:14:28,833
<i>I think you can.</i>

289
00:14:28,916 --> 00:14:30,791
<i>And you want Noah to live, don't you?</i>

290
00:14:30,875 --> 00:14:33,083
Noah has nothing to do with this! Please--

291
00:14:33,166 --> 00:14:34,958
-[shrill electronic whine]
-[gasps]

292
00:14:35,041 --> 00:14:37,416
-[whining continues]
-[Maia groaning]

293
00:14:38,208 --> 00:14:39,250
[bird squawks]

294
00:14:39,333 --> 00:14:41,083
[panting]

295
00:14:41,166 --> 00:14:42,500
[mobile phone chimes]

296
00:15:02,916 --> 00:15:04,500
I'm sorry I bored you.

297
00:15:06,291 --> 00:15:07,791
I'll do whatever you say.

298
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,708
-[Noah] <i>Thank you, Mummy.</i>
-Noah?

299
00:15:10,791 --> 00:15:12,208
<i>-I like your friend.</i>
-[static whines]

300
00:15:12,291 --> 00:15:13,875
<i>Can he be my daddy, please?</i>

301
00:15:13,958 --> 00:15:16,750
-What?
<i>-Can he be my daddy, please?</i>

302
00:15:16,833 --> 00:15:18,000
[distorted] <i>Can he be my daddy, please?</i>

303
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:19,291
Hello? Are you all right?

304
00:15:22,541 --> 00:15:24,541
[caller chuckles] <i>Isn't AI amazing?</i>

305
00:15:25,291 --> 00:15:26,708
<i>Irresponsible to have unleashed it</i>

306
00:15:26,791 --> 00:15:28,333
<i>on the general public, really.</i>

307
00:15:29,583 --> 00:15:31,375
<i>You should check his glucose numbers.</i>

308
00:15:35,666 --> 00:15:37,166
[beeping]

309
00:15:37,250 --> 00:15:39,166
<i>Thirty-two's quite low, isn't it?</i>

310
00:15:40,916 --> 00:15:43,416
You… You hacked his insulin dispenser?

311
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:45,291
<i>I gave him an extra dose.</i>

312
00:15:45,375 --> 00:15:47,625
<i>And now he's in a hypoglycaemic coma.</i>

313
00:15:55,875 --> 00:15:57,750
{\an8}[shudders]

314
00:16:02,208 --> 00:16:04,166
{\an8}<i>Another full dose would kill him.</i>

315
00:16:04,916 --> 00:16:06,333
{\an8}<i>But this drip is quite slow.</i>

316
00:16:07,625 --> 00:16:10,583
{\an8}<i>He should survive for about an hour.</i>

317
00:16:13,291 --> 00:16:15,166
{\an8}-[Maia gasps]
<i>-The coma is reversible</i>

318
00:16:15,250 --> 00:16:17,083
{\an8}<i>with an injection of glucagon,</i>

319
00:16:17,166 --> 00:16:19,375
{\an8}<i>which I know you always carry with you.</i>

320
00:16:21,583 --> 00:16:23,750
<i>You're going to kill Tafa</i>

321
00:16:23,833 --> 00:16:27,291
<i>and only then will I tell you</i>
<i>where Noah is.</i>

322
00:16:28,125 --> 00:16:29,375
[sniffles]

323
00:16:30,125 --> 00:16:31,541
[breath trembles]

324
00:16:32,291 --> 00:16:33,875
<i>Now, text Ted.</i>

325
00:16:33,958 --> 00:16:35,125
<i>Tell him you need to see Tafa</i>

326
00:16:35,208 --> 00:16:37,375
<i>for some last-minute trial advice.</i>

327
00:16:38,750 --> 00:16:40,875
[sniffs, exhales]

328
00:16:53,875 --> 00:16:55,375
<i>Let me send that for you.</i>

329
00:16:58,583 --> 00:17:01,083
[breathing heavily]

330
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:07,583
<i>From where you're standing,</i>

331
00:17:07,666 --> 00:17:10,791
<i>it's just over five miles</i>
<i>to the Excelsus Hotel.</i>

332
00:17:10,875 --> 00:17:12,125
<i>-At your pace…</i>
-Wait…

333
00:17:12,208 --> 00:17:14,000
<i>…you can cover that in under an hour.</i>

334
00:17:14,083 --> 00:17:15,625
You want me to run?

335
00:17:15,708 --> 00:17:18,333
<i>Keeping you running keeps you</i>
<i>where I can track you.</i>

336
00:17:18,416 --> 00:17:20,708
<i>Stops you from talking</i>
<i>to anyone you shouldn't.</i>

337
00:17:22,375 --> 00:17:23,541
Please.

338
00:17:23,625 --> 00:17:25,333
<i>And you know what happens</i>
<i>if you break the rules.</i>

339
00:17:25,416 --> 00:17:27,583
-Stop!
-[watch vibrates]

340
00:17:28,583 --> 00:17:31,583
-[beeping]
<i>-Tick, tick, tick, tick…</i>

341
00:17:37,666 --> 00:17:40,000
[child's laughter echoes]

342
00:17:41,500 --> 00:17:42,708
[dog barking]

343
00:17:44,041 --> 00:17:45,791
[birds' cries echo]

344
00:17:45,875 --> 00:17:47,833
-[exhales]
<i>-Maia?</i>

345
00:17:47,916 --> 00:17:49,291
[beeping]

346
00:17:49,375 --> 00:17:51,208
You're wasting time.

347
00:17:55,583 --> 00:17:56,666
<i>Maia!</i>

348
00:17:56,750 --> 00:17:58,458
[tense music playing]

349
00:18:25,375 --> 00:18:27,333
[reporter] <i>There's a palpable</i>
<i>air of expectation</i>

350
00:18:27,416 --> 00:18:28,875
<i>here at the Old Bailey today</i>

351
00:18:28,958 --> 00:18:31,000
<i>on the opening day of Tommy Boyd's trial</i>

352
00:18:31,083 --> 00:18:32,666
<i>for double murder.</i>

353
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:35,458
<i>Mr Boyd, an alleged crime boss</i>
<i>in south London,</i>

354
00:18:35,541 --> 00:18:36,583
<i>is accused of murdering</i>

355
00:18:36,666 --> 00:18:38,833
<i>Sasha Summerhill and Anita Patel</i>

356
00:18:38,916 --> 00:18:41,500
<i>after an altercation</i>
<i>at a night spot in Romford.</i>

357
00:18:44,958 --> 00:18:47,083
{\an8}[beeping]

358
00:18:55,208 --> 00:18:56,541
[Maia panting]

359
00:18:56,625 --> 00:18:58,416
[tense music playing]

360
00:19:13,875 --> 00:19:15,125
Oh. Hey! Hey, Maia.

361
00:19:15,208 --> 00:19:17,958
Hey! Oh, I'm so glad I ran into you.

362
00:19:18,041 --> 00:19:21,916
I wanted to apologise for Weston's party.

363
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,041
I-I told him to ask the whole class, and…

364
00:19:24,125 --> 00:19:26,291
[caller] God, I loathe parental hypocrisy.

365
00:19:26,375 --> 00:19:29,291
But he binned Noah's invite
when I wasn't looking.

366
00:19:29,375 --> 00:19:31,750
[chuckles] You know how silly boys can be.

367
00:19:31,833 --> 00:19:33,708
[caller] <i>Call her a bitch.</i>
<i>It's what you're thinking.</i>

368
00:19:33,791 --> 00:19:35,666
…not talking to each other.

369
00:19:35,750 --> 00:19:36,833
<i>-Do it.</i>
-I did ask Weston why.

370
00:19:36,916 --> 00:19:38,625
-And he said--
-Bitch.

371
00:19:38,708 --> 00:19:40,250
[woman] Oh, my God. How rude!

372
00:19:40,333 --> 00:19:41,500
[woman 2] What's she on about?

373
00:19:41,583 --> 00:19:44,291
[caller] <i>Doesn't that feel</i>
<i>good, to be yourself?</i>

374
00:19:44,375 --> 00:19:46,458
-[Alice] What's that about?
-[woman 1] Are you all right?

375
00:19:46,541 --> 00:19:48,791
<i>Keep going straight, down College Lane.</i>

376
00:19:49,541 --> 00:19:51,416
[Maia panting]

377
00:19:53,791 --> 00:19:55,625
{\an8}[monitor beeping]

378
00:19:55,708 --> 00:19:57,583
{\an8}Your heart rate is elevated.

379
00:19:57,666 --> 00:19:59,208
<i>You need to pace yourself.</i>

380
00:20:10,625 --> 00:20:12,875
Under-16 pentathlon champ.

381
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:16,458
You'd do anything to win, wouldn't you?

382
00:20:17,208 --> 00:20:18,541
Is that immigrant drive

383
00:20:18,625 --> 00:20:20,541
or having your father as your coach?

384
00:20:24,541 --> 00:20:26,791
<i>What was it he said to you?</i>

385
00:20:26,875 --> 00:20:28,000
<i>"Control your breath,</i>

386
00:20:29,083 --> 00:20:30,541
<i>master your fear."</i>

387
00:20:31,916 --> 00:20:34,125
<i>-Good advice.</i>
-You don't know me.

388
00:20:34,208 --> 00:20:35,666
That's where you're wrong, Maia.

389
00:20:37,458 --> 00:20:39,750
I know you better than you know yourself.

390
00:20:40,833 --> 00:20:42,708
[suspenseful music playing]

391
00:20:46,875 --> 00:20:48,500
[indistinct overlapping chatter]

392
00:20:49,708 --> 00:20:51,625
-[women wailing]
-Hey, stop!

393
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:56,791
[women wailing]

394
00:21:06,250 --> 00:21:08,125
[Maia panting]

395
00:21:14,875 --> 00:21:16,750
<i>Do you know what piqued</i>
<i>my interest in you?</i>

396
00:21:16,833 --> 00:21:18,291
-[brakes squealing]
-[Maia grunts]

397
00:21:18,375 --> 00:21:19,500
[cyclist] You okay?

398
00:21:19,583 --> 00:21:21,000
[caller] <i>Why would such</i>
<i>an attractive woman</i>

399
00:21:21,083 --> 00:21:22,791
<i>choose to have a child on her own?</i>

400
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:27,333
<i>You've been running</i>
<i>from your past, haven't you?</i>

401
00:21:29,333 --> 00:21:31,291
{\an8}Hard to lose a parent to violent crime.

402
00:21:32,333 --> 00:21:34,541
Harder still when
the killer is your mother.

403
00:21:36,416 --> 00:21:37,583
All those birthdays on your own

404
00:21:37,666 --> 00:21:39,083
while she was in prison.

405
00:21:39,166 --> 00:21:40,458
She didn't do it.

406
00:21:41,250 --> 00:21:42,250
She was innocent.

407
00:21:42,333 --> 00:21:44,208
Why lie to yourself, Maia?

408
00:21:44,291 --> 00:21:46,166
I'm sure he abused her terribly.

409
00:21:46,250 --> 00:21:48,583
I'm not gonna…

410
00:21:48,666 --> 00:21:51,000
I'm not gonna talk about
my private life with you.

411
00:21:51,083 --> 00:21:53,333
{\an8}[caller] Well, opening up is a process.

412
00:21:54,166 --> 00:21:55,416
{\an8}We'll get there.

413
00:21:56,875 --> 00:21:59,541
But tell me, is that
why you became a lawyer

414
00:22:00,541 --> 00:22:03,125
to assert your will over violent men?

415
00:22:04,125 --> 00:22:05,625
-I became a lawyer to--
-[dog barking]

416
00:22:05,708 --> 00:22:07,416
-[gasps, grunts]
-[woman] I'm so sorry.

417
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:09,500
To put psychopaths like you in jail.

418
00:22:10,958 --> 00:22:11,958
[laughs]

419
00:22:19,083 --> 00:22:21,583
[caller] <i>Cross the street</i>
<i>and go down Kentish Town Road.</i>

420
00:22:28,125 --> 00:22:29,125
<i>Just a little reminder,</i>

421
00:22:30,666 --> 00:22:33,333
<i>you've got 53 minutes,</i>
<i>10 seconds remaining.</i>

422
00:22:33,416 --> 00:22:35,833
[timer beeping]

423
00:22:35,916 --> 00:22:38,291
-[suspenseful music plays]
-[Maia panting]

424
00:22:46,291 --> 00:22:47,291
[indistinct chatter]

425
00:22:47,375 --> 00:22:48,375
[man] Let me know…

426
00:22:50,708 --> 00:22:52,666
<i>Why are you slowing down? What's going on?</i>

427
00:22:53,833 --> 00:22:55,833
It's crowded. Everyone's on their phones.

428
00:22:55,916 --> 00:22:57,125
[woman] They know she was fortunate.

429
00:22:57,208 --> 00:22:58,666
[caller] <i>That's the world we live in.</i>

430
00:22:59,208 --> 00:23:02,750
<i>Nobody meets your eye,</i>
<i>all staring at a device.</i>

431
00:23:02,833 --> 00:23:04,666
Mind you, Kentish town at rush hour

432
00:23:04,750 --> 00:23:06,500
is always full of nutters.

433
00:23:11,583 --> 00:23:12,875
So you live locally.

434
00:23:13,541 --> 00:23:16,083
<i>Huh! Don't try to be clever, Maia.</i>

435
00:23:18,708 --> 00:23:20,166
I recognise the gun.

436
00:23:20,750 --> 00:23:21,750
<i>Oh, really?</i>

437
00:23:21,833 --> 00:23:23,083
Ruger LCP,

438
00:23:23,166 --> 00:23:24,416
the same model your employer used

439
00:23:24,500 --> 00:23:26,041
to murder those women.

440
00:23:26,125 --> 00:23:27,708
<i>No, you've missed the point.</i>

441
00:23:28,666 --> 00:23:30,041
It's the exact same gun.

442
00:23:30,750 --> 00:23:33,333
You and I are gonna drive
the conspiracy nuts wild.

443
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,958
But I will give you this.

444
00:23:38,041 --> 00:23:40,916
No one but you could have
got Tafa to squeal.

445
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:42,875
{\an8}That was impressive.

446
00:23:49,750 --> 00:23:51,708
{\an8}The rest of your case is pathetic.

447
00:23:53,416 --> 00:23:54,875
So once you've killed Tafa,

448
00:23:56,416 --> 00:23:58,458
my client will walk.

449
00:23:59,125 --> 00:24:00,458
[Maia] <i>You sick prick.</i>

450
00:24:01,166 --> 00:24:02,333
[caller] Don't torment yourself.

451
00:24:02,416 --> 00:24:03,791
Tafa's no angel.

452
00:24:03,875 --> 00:24:06,166
No, but Tafa doesn't rape

453
00:24:06,250 --> 00:24:08,000
and murder women like your boss.

454
00:24:08,083 --> 00:24:11,791
Ah, there she is, the fearless
champion of wronged women.

455
00:24:12,750 --> 00:24:15,875
Will that be the title of your
self-righteous autobiography?

456
00:24:15,958 --> 00:24:17,833
[Maia] <i>Are you some sort of woman hater?</i>

457
00:24:20,250 --> 00:24:22,041
I'm gonna give those murdered women

458
00:24:22,125 --> 00:24:24,125
a voice in front of a jury,

459
00:24:24,208 --> 00:24:25,958
<i>then the law will come for you.</i>

460
00:24:26,833 --> 00:24:28,041
I am the law, Maia.

461
00:24:29,541 --> 00:24:31,250
<i>Might is right these days.</i>

462
00:24:34,666 --> 00:24:36,083
I know you didn't go home.

463
00:24:37,458 --> 00:24:39,708
-What?
-You said you took Noah home,

464
00:24:39,791 --> 00:24:41,000
but you can't have.

465
00:24:41,083 --> 00:24:42,458
I heard piano music and voices.

466
00:24:42,541 --> 00:24:44,041
Maia, you're remedial.

467
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:48,375
And you must have an accomplice.

468
00:24:48,458 --> 00:24:51,250
You didn't have time
to drop Noah's bag yourself,

469
00:24:51,333 --> 00:24:53,125
<i>which means there's someone out--</i>

470
00:24:53,208 --> 00:24:55,458
You're boring me again, Maia.

471
00:24:55,541 --> 00:24:57,166
-[insect buzzing]
-[glass tinkling]

472
00:24:59,625 --> 00:25:01,875
[mobile phone ringing]

473
00:25:01,958 --> 00:25:03,500
[automated voice] <i>Noah's school calling.</i>

474
00:25:04,375 --> 00:25:05,541
[AI Maia] <i>Hello?</i>

475
00:25:05,625 --> 00:25:08,541
<i>Hi, Maia. Er, this is Malcolm Brady.</i>

476
00:25:08,625 --> 00:25:10,666
<i>Erm, look, Noah wasn't</i>
<i>at registration this morning.</i>

477
00:25:10,750 --> 00:25:13,375
-Hello? Hello? He--
<i>-Is everything okay?</i>

478
00:25:13,458 --> 00:25:15,291
[AI Maia] <i>Oh, I completely</i>
<i>forgot to call you.</i>

479
00:25:15,375 --> 00:25:17,500
-[keyboard clacking]
<i>-I'm sorry.</i>

480
00:25:17,583 --> 00:25:20,083
<i>He's feeling poorly</i>
<i>and I kept him at home.</i>

481
00:25:21,083 --> 00:25:22,083
[Malcolm] <i>Oh, I see.</i>

482
00:25:22,166 --> 00:25:24,750
<i>Do you mind letting us know</i>
<i>in future so we don't worry?</i>

483
00:25:26,083 --> 00:25:27,125
[AI Maia] <i>I'm glad he has a teacher</i>

484
00:25:27,208 --> 00:25:28,500
<i>who worries over him.</i>

485
00:25:31,750 --> 00:25:34,208
<i>Sorry, I'd talk more, but I've got to run.</i>

486
00:25:36,250 --> 00:25:37,666
<i>Bye.</i>

487
00:25:40,708 --> 00:25:42,250
[caller] <i>That should buy us some time.</i>

488
00:25:42,916 --> 00:25:43,958
<i>Let's go.</i>

489
00:25:46,708 --> 00:25:47,875
[man] I'll be there by 12:00.

490
00:25:50,708 --> 00:25:53,000
-[beeping]
-[caller] <i>Tick, tick, tick.</i>

491
00:26:00,291 --> 00:26:01,291
[tyres screech]

492
00:26:01,375 --> 00:26:03,291
What are you doing?
Look where you're going!

493
00:26:03,375 --> 00:26:05,041
What is going on with people today?

494
00:26:05,125 --> 00:26:06,958
[customer] Just got lucky.

495
00:26:10,708 --> 00:26:13,041
[overlapping chatter]

496
00:26:23,166 --> 00:26:24,166
<i>Go straight ahead.</i>

497
00:26:27,875 --> 00:26:29,166
[workman] Hey, what's the rush, darling?

498
00:26:32,750 --> 00:26:34,500
[caller] Where are you going?
I said straight ahead.

499
00:26:34,583 --> 00:26:36,541
[Maia] <i>It's gonna be quicker</i>
<i>along the canal.</i>

500
00:26:38,208 --> 00:26:39,458
[caller] <i>Remember the rules, Maia.</i>

501
00:26:39,541 --> 00:26:40,791
<i>You do what I say.</i>

502
00:26:40,875 --> 00:26:44,250
Trust me, I'm the one
who actually runs in the city.

503
00:26:45,958 --> 00:26:48,041
[street vendors yelling]

504
00:26:49,583 --> 00:26:50,666
[vendor] Sale!

505
00:26:52,875 --> 00:26:53,958
[overlapping chatter]

506
00:27:05,458 --> 00:27:06,750
[speaks other language]

507
00:27:07,625 --> 00:27:08,875
[woman gasps]

508
00:27:08,958 --> 00:27:10,458
[male pedestrian in English]
She's a thief!

509
00:27:10,541 --> 00:27:12,750
-[caller] <i>What was that?</i>
-I bumped into someone.

510
00:27:19,833 --> 00:27:21,833
{\an8}[overlapping chatter continues]

511
00:27:24,375 --> 00:27:26,500
[vendor 1] I see you're
interested. Come on, fella.

512
00:27:26,583 --> 00:27:27,666
[vendor 2] They're making it right…

513
00:27:37,916 --> 00:27:39,250
[pedestrian yells]

514
00:27:39,333 --> 00:27:42,541
-Hey, my phone!
-[man] Oi!

515
00:27:42,625 --> 00:27:44,750
She's got my phone! You lot, stop her!

516
00:27:48,708 --> 00:27:50,375
Hey, come back here!

517
00:27:50,458 --> 00:27:52,708
[panting]

518
00:27:52,791 --> 00:27:54,458
She's got my phone!

519
00:27:57,041 --> 00:27:58,083
Give me back my phone!

520
00:27:58,166 --> 00:27:59,916
[indistinct chattering in other language]

521
00:28:01,916 --> 00:28:04,041
[caller, in English] <i>I dislike</i>
<i>it when you're quiet.</i>

522
00:28:04,125 --> 00:28:05,125
<i>What's on your mind?</i>

523
00:28:05,208 --> 00:28:06,250
What the hell are you doing?

524
00:28:06,333 --> 00:28:07,416
[man speaks in other language]

525
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:10,125
[in English] I'm wondering whether or not

526
00:28:10,208 --> 00:28:12,750
Noah has spoiled his dinner
with all that ice cream.

527
00:28:15,500 --> 00:28:17,000
<i>You've got a sense of humour.</i>

528
00:28:18,250 --> 00:28:20,083
<i>Do you think your beautiful</i>
<i>boy will inherit that?</i>

529
00:28:23,208 --> 00:28:25,291
I know Noah's father was only a donor,

530
00:28:26,125 --> 00:28:28,291
<i>-but will he ever meet him?</i>
-No.

531
00:28:30,541 --> 00:28:31,708
Probably for the best.

532
00:28:32,583 --> 00:28:34,208
<i>Fathers are tricky, aren't they?</i>

533
00:28:36,750 --> 00:28:39,958
[boyfriend] All right, now
this angle… this looks good.

534
00:28:41,500 --> 00:28:42,750
-[gasps]
-[boy] What are you doing?

535
00:28:42,833 --> 00:28:44,750
-Stop! Bring that back!
-[girl] She took my phone!

536
00:28:44,833 --> 00:28:46,166
-[boy] Yo!
-[girl] Oi! Stop her!

537
00:28:46,250 --> 00:28:47,541
[boy] That's my girl's phone!

538
00:28:50,125 --> 00:28:51,250
Stop!

539
00:28:52,125 --> 00:28:53,583
-Stop!
-[people exclaim]

540
00:28:58,875 --> 00:28:59,958
Stop!

541
00:29:01,583 --> 00:29:04,333
That's my girl's phone! Hey, stop!

542
00:29:05,375 --> 00:29:06,500
Please…

543
00:29:06,583 --> 00:29:07,708
You all right, love?

544
00:29:08,708 --> 00:29:10,250
-Oi! Hey, hey, hey!
-[boy] Oi!

545
00:29:10,333 --> 00:29:11,333
That's my girl's phone!

546
00:29:11,416 --> 00:29:12,791
-Oi! Oi!
-[builder] Whoa!

547
00:29:12,875 --> 00:29:14,375
-What are you talking about?
-That's my phone!

548
00:29:14,458 --> 00:29:16,750
That's my girl's phone!
You've got the wrong guy!

549
00:29:16,833 --> 00:29:18,458
That's my girl's phone!

550
00:29:18,541 --> 00:29:21,333
Oi! You got the wrong guy!
She's got my phone.

551
00:29:22,375 --> 00:29:24,083
{\an8}-[grunts] Are you kidding me?
-Sorry.

552
00:29:24,166 --> 00:29:26,291
{\an8}[Maia panting]

553
00:29:34,458 --> 00:29:36,500
{\an8}[woman talks indistinctly]

554
00:29:36,583 --> 00:29:37,958
{\an8}[mid-tempo song playing on speakers]

555
00:29:38,041 --> 00:29:39,583
{\an8}[woman] Hey, watch out!

556
00:29:39,666 --> 00:29:41,208
{\an8}[Maia grunts] No!

557
00:29:41,875 --> 00:29:42,875
Shit!

558
00:29:42,958 --> 00:29:44,291
[woman] What's wrong with you?

559
00:29:44,375 --> 00:29:46,000
-[child crying]
-Watch where you're going!

560
00:29:47,458 --> 00:29:49,291
[woman soothes child]

561
00:29:50,333 --> 00:29:51,583
[caller] <i>Maia?</i>

562
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:55,000
<i>Maia?</i>

563
00:29:55,083 --> 00:29:56,458
[Maia] I fell.

564
00:29:57,125 --> 00:29:58,583
<i>You okay?</i>

565
00:29:58,666 --> 00:29:59,916
I hurt my knee.

566
00:30:01,625 --> 00:30:02,625
<i>Is it serious?</i>

567
00:30:03,625 --> 00:30:04,958
[sighs] As if you care.

568
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:09,000
Oh, but I do care.
You're very precious to me.

569
00:30:10,250 --> 00:30:11,541
<i>And to Ted.</i>

570
00:30:12,833 --> 00:30:13,958
<i>He was really upset</i>

571
00:30:14,041 --> 00:30:15,416
<i>by your conversation this morning.</i>

572
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:17,500
You've hacked into Ted's phone.

573
00:30:18,791 --> 00:30:19,791
An insurance policy,

574
00:30:19,875 --> 00:30:21,458
in case you were
foolish enough to contact him.

575
00:30:22,041 --> 00:30:23,375
Hmm?

576
00:30:23,458 --> 00:30:25,791
<i>You know what he told</i>
<i>his friend Alan yesterday?</i>

577
00:30:25,875 --> 00:30:27,708
<i>He said he feels something with you</i>

578
00:30:27,791 --> 00:30:29,833
<i>that he's never felt with a woman before.</i>

579
00:30:32,583 --> 00:30:35,041
<i>But I wonder if you might</i>
<i>just be toying with him.</i>

580
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:38,666
<i>All those flirty texts,</i>
<i>which you never follow up on.</i>

581
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:44,083
You know, I, um…

582
00:30:44,166 --> 00:30:46,666
I found a folder on your laptop.

583
00:30:47,916 --> 00:30:49,458
You thought you deleted it.

584
00:30:50,458 --> 00:30:52,583
But your digital hygiene is terrible.

585
00:30:55,250 --> 00:30:56,250
Were those photos for him?

586
00:30:56,333 --> 00:30:57,750
[breathing heavily]

587
00:31:01,625 --> 00:31:03,791
[breathing sounds intensify]

588
00:31:07,416 --> 00:31:09,000
You little piece of shit.

589
00:31:09,083 --> 00:31:11,708
You perv. You freaking perv.

590
00:31:20,583 --> 00:31:23,250
<i>You're so avoidant, Maia. It's unhealthy.</i>

591
00:31:25,666 --> 00:31:27,208
<i>Have you ever seen a therapist?</i>

592
00:31:27,750 --> 00:31:29,750
<i>-Oh, wait. Yes, Dr Katz.</i>
-Shit.

593
00:31:30,375 --> 00:31:32,208
<i>But that didn't last for long.</i>

594
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:34,208
<i>Painful, was it?</i>

595
00:31:34,958 --> 00:31:37,458
<i>But we all need to share</i>
<i>our secrets with someone.</i>

596
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:41,791
<i>Why did you use an encrypted app</i>

597
00:31:41,875 --> 00:31:43,458
<i>to communicate with your mother?</i>

598
00:31:44,333 --> 00:31:46,333
<i>And what does this message</i>
<i>mean where she says,</i>

599
00:31:46,416 --> 00:31:49,125
<i>"We're forever bonded</i>
<i>by what happened that night"?</i>

600
00:31:50,250 --> 00:31:51,250
[insect buzzing]

601
00:31:52,333 --> 00:31:53,583
<i>Did you see the body?</i>

602
00:31:54,416 --> 00:31:56,416
Or did she shelter you from it?

603
00:31:57,833 --> 00:32:00,458
<i>"What's bred in the bone</i>
<i>outs in the flesh."</i>

604
00:32:01,541 --> 00:32:04,291
{\an8}Do you know what that
expression means, Maia?

605
00:32:04,375 --> 00:32:06,708
{\an8}It means you can't escape who you are.

606
00:32:06,791 --> 00:32:08,041
Leave me alone.

607
00:32:09,541 --> 00:32:11,375
[caller] <i>That's why I think</i>
<i>you've got what it takes.</i>

608
00:32:12,291 --> 00:32:14,375
<i>You're worried</i>
<i>that you're like your mother,</i>

609
00:32:14,458 --> 00:32:15,875
<i>and she was a killer.</i>

610
00:32:16,750 --> 00:32:18,333
<i>And you think you are, too.</i>

611
00:32:18,416 --> 00:32:20,708
[Maia] <i>She wasn't a killer. You're wrong.</i>

612
00:32:20,791 --> 00:32:22,583
<i>Come on, Maia, tell me the truth.</i>

613
00:32:23,916 --> 00:32:26,583
<i>All I want is honesty.</i>
<i>What happened to your father?</i>

614
00:32:26,666 --> 00:32:27,833
-Ugh! Get out of my--
-[tyres screech]

615
00:32:27,916 --> 00:32:29,041
[woman screams]

616
00:32:29,125 --> 00:32:30,708
[electronic whine]

617
00:32:36,500 --> 00:32:37,916
[whooshing]

618
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:39,791
[paramedic, distorted]
I'm just checking your eyes.

619
00:32:39,875 --> 00:32:41,166
[caller] <i>Maia.</i>

620
00:32:41,250 --> 00:32:42,291
[paramedic] You were in an accident.

621
00:32:42,375 --> 00:32:43,416
[caller] <i>Maia.</i>

622
00:32:43,500 --> 00:32:45,458
[paramedic] Everything's going to be fine.

623
00:32:45,541 --> 00:32:46,708
<i>Maia, where are you?</i>

624
00:32:46,791 --> 00:32:48,958
[paramedic] I'm getting you
to hospital, okay?

625
00:32:50,416 --> 00:32:52,583
Everything's going to be fine.

626
00:32:53,791 --> 00:32:57,083
[caller] <i>Are you okay? Maia, wake up!</i>

627
00:32:57,166 --> 00:32:58,375
[paramedic] Okay?

628
00:32:58,458 --> 00:33:00,375
How… How long have I been…

629
00:33:01,500 --> 00:33:03,041
You were hit by a car.

630
00:33:03,666 --> 00:33:05,625
You've been unconscious for a few minutes.

631
00:33:07,791 --> 00:33:08,791
Well…

632
00:33:08,875 --> 00:33:10,166
[caller] <i>Ah, I'm glad to have you back.</i>

633
00:33:10,250 --> 00:33:11,583
Noah…

634
00:33:11,666 --> 00:33:15,291
<i>But you've lost a lot of time.</i>
<i>The clock is ticking.</i>

635
00:33:18,083 --> 00:33:19,208
I can't do this.

636
00:33:19,875 --> 00:33:21,083
I need to rest.

637
00:33:21,750 --> 00:33:25,083
[caller] <i>Come on, Maia,</i>
<i>you're a fighter. Fight!</i>

638
00:33:29,208 --> 00:33:31,750
[Maia groans] I have to run.

639
00:33:31,833 --> 00:33:33,416
-Oh! Oh! Er…
-I can't do this,

640
00:33:33,500 --> 00:33:34,666
I need to run.

641
00:33:34,750 --> 00:33:36,583
I need to run. I need to run.

642
00:33:36,666 --> 00:33:38,375
-Listen…
-I'm gonna get you a sedative.

643
00:33:38,458 --> 00:33:40,416
I need to go. Dammit.

644
00:33:40,500 --> 00:33:41,833
-Please calm down!
-Let me go!

645
00:33:41,916 --> 00:33:43,666
I'm trying to help you!

646
00:33:43,750 --> 00:33:45,000
-What are you doing?
-[siren blaring]

647
00:33:45,083 --> 00:33:46,791
-You should be in hospital!
-[passer-by] Oh, bugger!

648
00:33:46,875 --> 00:33:48,125
Stop! Stop the van!

649
00:33:48,875 --> 00:33:49,875
[tyres screech]

650
00:33:52,500 --> 00:33:53,666
[woman] Hey!

651
00:33:54,458 --> 00:33:57,166
[caller] <i>You have 35 minutes,</i>
<i>20 seconds remaining.</i>

652
00:34:00,166 --> 00:34:01,208
I need more time.

653
00:34:01,791 --> 00:34:03,583
I need more time. I won't make it.

654
00:34:04,458 --> 00:34:06,000
<i>There is no more time.</i>

655
00:34:06,083 --> 00:34:08,041
[retches]

656
00:34:08,125 --> 00:34:09,916
<i>Witness protection will pick up Tafa</i>

657
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:11,833
<i>at 10:15 precisely.</i>

658
00:34:12,708 --> 00:34:14,583
<i>If you're going to save Noah,</i>

659
00:34:14,666 --> 00:34:16,750
<i>you need to be there 15 minutes before.</i>

660
00:34:16,833 --> 00:34:18,041
[unsettling music plays]

661
00:34:22,166 --> 00:34:24,125
[unsettling music continues]

662
00:34:24,208 --> 00:34:25,458
[panting]

663
00:34:32,666 --> 00:34:34,166
[beeping]

664
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:38,625
Ah, you've got to pick up the pace, Maia.

665
00:34:47,708 --> 00:34:49,625
[man grunts] What do
you think you're doing?

666
00:34:49,708 --> 00:34:50,916
[ticket barrier alarm blaring]

667
00:34:55,583 --> 00:34:57,375
[train doors beeping]

668
00:34:59,333 --> 00:35:00,791
[baby crying]

669
00:35:02,416 --> 00:35:03,958
[announcer] <i>…City Line train to Barking.</i>

670
00:35:04,666 --> 00:35:07,083
<i>The next station is Farringdon.</i>

671
00:35:09,791 --> 00:35:12,083
[overlapping chatter]

672
00:35:17,958 --> 00:35:19,291
[shrill screeching]

673
00:35:19,375 --> 00:35:20,541
[caller] What's that noise?

674
00:35:20,625 --> 00:35:21,875
{\an8}-[baby crying]
-[headset beeps]

675
00:35:21,958 --> 00:35:23,041
{\an8}[ambient noise becomes muffled]

676
00:35:23,958 --> 00:35:25,750
{\an8}-[crying intensifies]
-[caller winces] Ow!

677
00:35:27,916 --> 00:35:30,208
[crying continues on headset]

678
00:35:30,291 --> 00:35:32,208
It's okay.

679
00:35:34,541 --> 00:35:35,791
[mother] Aww!

680
00:35:42,375 --> 00:35:43,625
It's all right.

681
00:35:44,416 --> 00:35:45,958
It's okay.

682
00:35:49,666 --> 00:35:51,000
[commuter talks indistinctly]

683
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:54,375
[caller grunts softly]

684
00:35:56,416 --> 00:35:57,458
[exhales]

685
00:35:57,541 --> 00:35:58,916
[commuter] Do you know
if this train goes to Bank?

686
00:36:02,083 --> 00:36:03,958
[map beeping]

687
00:36:04,875 --> 00:36:06,166
[caller] You're going very fast.

688
00:36:06,250 --> 00:36:07,333
<i>What's going on?</i>

689
00:36:08,833 --> 00:36:11,375
<i>I hope you're not breaking the rules.</i>

690
00:36:11,458 --> 00:36:12,958
No, I'm just trying to make up time.

691
00:36:25,583 --> 00:36:26,791
<i>Did your mother ever share with you</i>

692
00:36:26,875 --> 00:36:29,416
<i>what it was like to take a human's life?</i>

693
00:36:29,500 --> 00:36:32,083
-No.
<i>-Prepare yourself.</i>

694
00:36:32,166 --> 00:36:33,750
<i>There's more blood in the human body</i>

695
00:36:33,833 --> 00:36:34,833
<i>than you can fathom.</i>

696
00:36:35,666 --> 00:36:38,583
<i>And when it spills out,</i>
<i>you think it must be done.</i>

697
00:36:39,250 --> 00:36:40,666
<i>But it just keeps coming.</i>

698
00:36:40,750 --> 00:36:42,333
-[commuter preaching]
-I'm not interested!

699
00:36:42,416 --> 00:36:43,875
[commuter] …will have everlasting life,

700
00:36:43,958 --> 00:36:45,916
so that you can spend eternity in heaven.

701
00:36:48,250 --> 00:36:49,625
Not in hellfire.

702
00:36:49,708 --> 00:36:52,291
Do you want to give up
the desires of the flesh,

703
00:36:52,375 --> 00:36:54,166
and all its fleshly lusts,

704
00:36:54,250 --> 00:36:56,791
to spend your time with God the Father?

705
00:36:56,875 --> 00:36:57,875
[commuter 2] Watch it!

706
00:36:57,958 --> 00:36:59,125
[commuter] This is your opportunity today

707
00:36:59,208 --> 00:37:02,041
to repent and turn over a new leaf.

708
00:37:02,125 --> 00:37:05,125
[continues indistinctly]

709
00:37:09,666 --> 00:37:11,166
Okay.

710
00:37:12,541 --> 00:37:14,125
[caller] <i>Why are you slowing down again?</i>

711
00:37:14,208 --> 00:37:15,583
[Maia] Traffic.

712
00:37:16,833 --> 00:37:19,083
You don't want me to get run over, do you?

713
00:37:23,333 --> 00:37:26,291
[announcer] <i>The next station</i>
<i>is Farringdon.</i>

714
00:37:27,041 --> 00:37:31,666
<i>Change for the Elizabeth line</i>
<i>and National Rail services.</i>

715
00:37:34,958 --> 00:37:36,916
{\an8}[beeping steadily]

716
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:38,375
{\an8}[caller] You're not running, are you?

717
00:37:39,791 --> 00:37:40,875
I am.

718
00:37:41,666 --> 00:37:44,083
<i>-Are you on a train?</i>
-What? No.

719
00:37:44,166 --> 00:37:45,708
<i>Maia, do you think I'm stupid?</i>

720
00:37:45,791 --> 00:37:47,125
-What?
<i>-Think about your boy.</i>

721
00:37:47,208 --> 00:37:48,291
-[Maia] Hello? Hello?
-[both] Yeah!

722
00:37:48,375 --> 00:37:49,750
[static hisses]

723
00:37:49,833 --> 00:37:51,708
-Hello?
-[static hisses]

724
00:37:51,791 --> 00:37:52,791
Hello?

725
00:37:52,875 --> 00:37:53,875
[automated voice] <i>Connection lost.</i>

726
00:37:53,958 --> 00:37:55,000
[device chimes]

727
00:37:56,083 --> 00:37:57,458
[gasps]

728
00:37:57,541 --> 00:37:59,958
[Maia] My phone! My phone!

729
00:38:00,666 --> 00:38:01,916
My phone!

730
00:38:02,875 --> 00:38:04,666
-No, no, no, no!
-[both laugh mockingly]

731
00:38:04,750 --> 00:38:05,958
I need my phone!

732
00:38:06,041 --> 00:38:07,791
[panting] No, no!

733
00:38:14,833 --> 00:38:16,583
["Running" playing]

734
00:38:16,666 --> 00:38:20,541
[man] <i>♪ Wake me up</i>
<i>When the shooting starts ♪</i>

735
00:38:20,625 --> 00:38:22,625
<i>♪ I'm gonna pack my bag… ♪</i>

736
00:38:22,708 --> 00:38:23,916
[man] What are you doing?

737
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:26,750
-[tyres screech, horn blares]
-[taxi driver] Careful!

738
00:38:26,833 --> 00:38:29,208
<i>♪ Burn, burn, burn ♪</i>

739
00:38:29,291 --> 00:38:32,541
<i>♪ Burn, burn, burn</i>
<i>Burn, burn ♪</i>

740
00:38:32,625 --> 00:38:36,916
<i>♪ Let it burn, burn, burn</i>
<i>Burn, burn, burn ♪</i>

741
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:38,666
<i>♪ Let it burn ♪</i>

742
00:38:38,750 --> 00:38:40,541
<i>♪ Oh my God ♪</i>

743
00:38:40,625 --> 00:38:43,750
<i>♪ I was playing Lucy when</i>
<i>I should have played God ♪</i>

744
00:38:43,833 --> 00:38:46,583
-[horn blaring]
-[driver cries out]

745
00:38:46,666 --> 00:38:50,125
<i>♪ Only Lucy</i>
<i>Gonna hold me tight ♪</i>

746
00:38:50,208 --> 00:38:51,500
[tyres screech]

747
00:38:51,583 --> 00:38:52,625
[cab driver] Watch out, love!
Get off the road!

748
00:38:52,708 --> 00:38:55,083
<i>♪ I was playing Lucy when</i>
<i>I should have played God ♪</i>

749
00:38:55,166 --> 00:38:56,250
[dogs barking]

750
00:38:56,333 --> 00:38:58,625
<i>♪ Looking to the left</i>
<i>Should've been right ♪</i>

751
00:38:58,708 --> 00:39:00,625
-Come on!
-[horn blares]

752
00:39:01,416 --> 00:39:02,791
[tyres screech, brakes squeal]

753
00:39:05,083 --> 00:39:07,666
<i>♪ Running, running, running</i>
<i>Running, running ♪</i>

754
00:39:07,750 --> 00:39:10,291
<i>♪ Running, running</i>
<i>Running, running ♪</i>

755
00:39:10,375 --> 00:39:13,041
<i>♪ From the grey thoughts</i>
<i>In my mind ♪</i>

756
00:39:13,125 --> 00:39:14,208
[horns blaring]

757
00:39:14,291 --> 00:39:17,000
<i>♪ Running, running, running</i>
<i>Running, running ♪</i>

758
00:39:17,083 --> 00:39:19,541
<i>♪ Running, running, running</i>
<i>Running, running ♪</i>

759
00:39:19,625 --> 00:39:22,208
<i>♪ Running, running</i>
<i>Running, running ♪</i>

760
00:39:22,291 --> 00:39:24,541
<i>♪ From the grey thoughts</i>
<i>In my mind ♪</i>

761
00:39:24,625 --> 00:39:26,166
<i>♪ Don't blow me high ♪</i>

762
00:39:35,541 --> 00:39:38,750
<i>♪ I said blue back, baby ♪</i>

763
00:39:38,833 --> 00:39:40,791
<i>♪ On the telephone ♪</i>

764
00:39:41,833 --> 00:39:44,583
<i>♪ I'm in the calling light</i>
<i>Now, baby ♪</i>

765
00:39:44,666 --> 00:39:46,833
<i>♪ Won't you leave me alone? ♪</i>

766
00:39:48,375 --> 00:39:49,666
<i>♪ Bitch, I'm running ♪</i>

767
00:39:49,750 --> 00:39:52,750
<i>♪ Running, running</i>
<i>Running, running, running ♪</i>

768
00:39:52,833 --> 00:39:55,083
<i>♪ Running, running</i>
<i>Running, running, running ♪</i>

769
00:39:55,166 --> 00:39:57,291
<i>♪ Running, running, running ♪</i>

770
00:39:57,375 --> 00:39:59,833
<i>♪ From the grey thoughts</i>
<i>In my mind ♪</i>

771
00:39:59,916 --> 00:40:01,291
<i>♪ Bitch, I'm running ♪</i>

772
00:40:01,375 --> 00:40:04,750
<i>♪ Running, running, running</i>
<i>Running, running, running ♪</i>

773
00:40:04,833 --> 00:40:06,833
-[female commuter yells]
-Stop her!

774
00:40:06,916 --> 00:40:08,750
<i>♪ Running, running, running ♪</i>

775
00:40:08,833 --> 00:40:11,500
<i>♪ From the grey thoughts</i>
<i>In my mind ♪</i>

776
00:40:11,583 --> 00:40:12,791
<i>♪ Don't blow me high ♪</i>

777
00:40:12,875 --> 00:40:14,541
-[gasps]
-[music ends]

778
00:40:14,625 --> 00:40:16,833
[announcer] <i>…Central line</i>
<i>train to Barking.</i>

779
00:40:16,916 --> 00:40:19,583
<i>The next station is Liverpool Street.</i>

780
00:40:19,666 --> 00:40:21,750
[panting heavily]

781
00:40:29,291 --> 00:40:31,291
[train accelerating]

782
00:40:34,583 --> 00:40:36,833
[panting]

783
00:40:43,458 --> 00:40:45,458
[continues panting]

784
00:40:59,541 --> 00:41:00,583
[Maia] Hey.

785
00:41:01,416 --> 00:41:03,125
[thief 1] What?

786
00:41:06,458 --> 00:41:07,958
My phone.

787
00:41:08,041 --> 00:41:09,291
-What's she saying?
-[exhales sharply]

788
00:41:09,916 --> 00:41:12,291
-Whoa, hey.
-Give me my phone.

789
00:41:13,166 --> 00:41:14,791
Huh, what phone?

790
00:41:15,833 --> 00:41:17,291
Huh? [chuckling]

791
00:41:17,375 --> 00:41:18,916
What phone?

792
00:41:20,041 --> 00:41:21,333
Give it to me now.

793
00:41:21,416 --> 00:41:22,541
-Eh… Huh?
-[laughs]

794
00:41:22,625 --> 00:41:23,666
[pouch unzips]

795
00:41:26,458 --> 00:41:28,000
-[groans]
-[thief 2] Yo, what the heck?

796
00:41:29,291 --> 00:41:30,291
Chill out, lady!

797
00:41:30,375 --> 00:41:31,375
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

798
00:41:31,458 --> 00:41:32,458
[thief 2] Bro, she got a gun, man!

799
00:41:32,541 --> 00:41:33,666
[thief 1] What the hell?

800
00:41:34,166 --> 00:41:35,541
[commuters gasp]

801
00:41:36,666 --> 00:41:38,375
[woman] Oh, my God.

802
00:41:38,458 --> 00:41:40,416
[Maia panting]

803
00:41:43,291 --> 00:41:45,166
You have no idea what you've done.

804
00:41:47,416 --> 00:41:50,208
[radio chirps, indistinct radio chatter]

805
00:41:50,291 --> 00:41:51,583
[announcer] <i>The next station</i>
<i>is Liverpool Street.</i>

806
00:41:51,666 --> 00:41:52,958
Oh, shit.

807
00:41:53,041 --> 00:41:54,041
[male commuter] Is she all right?

808
00:41:54,125 --> 00:41:56,291
<i>Change for the Central and Circle lines,</i>

809
00:41:56,375 --> 00:41:59,625
<i>the Elizabeth line, London Overground…</i>

810
00:41:59,708 --> 00:42:00,875
[thief 1] She's got a friggin' gun, man.

811
00:42:00,958 --> 00:42:02,416
[officer] You okay?

812
00:42:02,500 --> 00:42:03,833
Ma'am?

813
00:42:05,458 --> 00:42:06,458
Ma'am?

814
00:42:12,166 --> 00:42:13,833
Stop, please, ma'am!

815
00:42:13,916 --> 00:42:15,833
[commuter grunts]

816
00:42:21,583 --> 00:42:23,916
[officer] Pull the emergency brake now!

817
00:42:29,333 --> 00:42:31,500
-[emergency brake squeals]
-[commuters yelling]

818
00:42:34,875 --> 00:42:35,916
[man] Sorry.

819
00:42:36,000 --> 00:42:38,708
[officer] What are you doing?
Don't go in there!

820
00:42:38,791 --> 00:42:39,791
Stop!

821
00:42:40,750 --> 00:42:42,125
Open up!

822
00:42:42,208 --> 00:42:44,416
Please, ma'am. Open up!

823
00:42:44,500 --> 00:42:46,958
Open this door! Open this door now!

824
00:42:47,041 --> 00:42:49,083
Open up, please, ma'am!

825
00:42:49,958 --> 00:42:51,750
Open up now!

826
00:43:00,125 --> 00:43:02,041
[panting]

827
00:43:06,083 --> 00:43:07,208
-[train whirring]
-[crackling]

828
00:43:10,583 --> 00:43:11,958
[train wheels clack]

829
00:43:24,875 --> 00:43:26,541
[train engine whining]

830
00:43:30,583 --> 00:43:32,625
[screams]

831
00:43:45,666 --> 00:43:48,416
[timer beeping]

832
00:43:55,750 --> 00:43:56,833
Hey. Hey!

833
00:43:58,666 --> 00:44:00,333
Hey, can you help me?

834
00:44:01,583 --> 00:44:03,666
Would you get off your goddamn phone?

835
00:44:03,750 --> 00:44:04,833
I need some help.

836
00:44:08,833 --> 00:44:10,333
-[man grunts]
-[Maia strains, grunts]

837
00:44:10,416 --> 00:44:11,666
[man] That's it.

838
00:44:11,750 --> 00:44:14,458
[announcer] <i>CCTV is in use</i>
<i>throughout London Underground.</i>

839
00:44:14,541 --> 00:44:16,458
[Maia panting]

840
00:44:20,916 --> 00:44:23,041
[sirens blaring]

841
00:44:26,333 --> 00:44:28,333
[female officer] Police! Move out the way!

842
00:44:28,416 --> 00:44:30,291
[indistinct police radio chatter]

843
00:44:30,375 --> 00:44:31,666
[officer 1] Back!

844
00:44:31,750 --> 00:44:33,625
Move, move, move!

845
00:44:33,708 --> 00:44:34,833
[officer 2] Evacuate the station!

846
00:44:34,916 --> 00:44:35,916
[officer 3] Police!

847
00:44:36,000 --> 00:44:37,375
<i>-♪ Kumbaya ♪</i>
-[officer 4] Move back!

848
00:44:38,083 --> 00:44:39,708
[officer 5] Police! Get back!

849
00:44:46,583 --> 00:44:47,583
[breath shudders]

850
00:44:51,000 --> 00:44:53,333
Come on, come on, come on.

851
00:44:53,416 --> 00:44:54,666
[mobile phone beeps]

852
00:44:54,750 --> 00:44:57,041
[Maia's breath trembles]

853
00:44:59,458 --> 00:45:01,125
[officer] Can we have a word
with you, love?

854
00:45:02,833 --> 00:45:03,958
Sure.

855
00:45:04,041 --> 00:45:05,833
Sure, sure, sure. [sniffles]

856
00:45:06,583 --> 00:45:08,166
Sorry.

857
00:45:08,250 --> 00:45:10,958
Is this, er, private property?

858
00:45:11,500 --> 00:45:13,666
I was just looking for some quiet place

859
00:45:13,750 --> 00:45:14,833
to call my boyfriend.

860
00:45:14,916 --> 00:45:17,750
Put your hands in the air
and lean against the wall.

861
00:45:17,833 --> 00:45:19,083
-[horn beeps]
-[cyclist whoops]

862
00:45:19,166 --> 00:45:21,000
-[officer] Stop! Stop! Police!
-[tense music playing]

863
00:45:23,416 --> 00:45:24,416
Stop! Police!

864
00:45:24,500 --> 00:45:25,625
[cyclists shouting indistinctly]

865
00:45:25,708 --> 00:45:27,000
[officer] Stop!

866
00:45:27,958 --> 00:45:29,916
Police! Get out my way!

867
00:45:31,250 --> 00:45:32,708
Stop! Stay where you are!

868
00:45:34,291 --> 00:45:35,625
[woman] Watch out!

869
00:45:35,708 --> 00:45:37,375
[people clamouring]

870
00:45:40,708 --> 00:45:41,958
[female cyclist shouts indistinctly]

871
00:45:42,041 --> 00:45:44,125
[upbeat song playing]

872
00:45:47,500 --> 00:45:48,583
[horn blares]

873
00:45:48,666 --> 00:45:49,958
Oh, my goodness! I almost hit you!

874
00:45:53,416 --> 00:45:54,833
[horns blaring]

875
00:45:56,666 --> 00:45:58,458
[officer] Hey, stop!

876
00:46:15,041 --> 00:46:16,041
[music ends]

877
00:46:16,125 --> 00:46:17,958
[panting]

878
00:46:27,375 --> 00:46:29,250
[mobile phone beeps]

879
00:46:32,041 --> 00:46:33,750
[sombre music playing]

880
00:46:42,500 --> 00:46:43,750
[Maia sobs]

881
00:46:53,333 --> 00:46:54,833
[priest] Are you all right?

882
00:46:56,791 --> 00:46:59,916
It's often those
who are afraid to ask for help

883
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:01,708
who need it the most.

884
00:47:03,000 --> 00:47:04,791
I just need a moment of peace.

885
00:47:09,208 --> 00:47:10,625
Would you like to confess?

886
00:47:13,375 --> 00:47:16,916
If you're in pain,
there are always options.

887
00:47:18,916 --> 00:47:20,416
[Maia whimpers]

888
00:47:20,500 --> 00:47:24,625
His blood is our blood,
and He bled for our sins.

889
00:47:27,291 --> 00:47:28,666
Did you know there's more blood

890
00:47:28,750 --> 00:47:31,000
in the human body than you can fathom?

891
00:47:34,500 --> 00:47:35,583
[suspenseful music playing]

892
00:47:35,666 --> 00:47:36,833
[door opens]

893
00:47:38,583 --> 00:47:40,291
[gasps]

894
00:47:46,083 --> 00:47:50,833
[choir singing]

895
00:48:00,333 --> 00:48:01,625
{\an8}[mobile phone ringing]

896
00:48:01,708 --> 00:48:03,583
{\an8}[automated voice] <i>Unknown caller calling.</i>

897
00:48:04,833 --> 00:48:06,333
Hello? I'm… I'm sorry.

898
00:48:06,416 --> 00:48:08,041
I'm sorry someone stole my phone.

899
00:48:08,125 --> 00:48:10,291
[scam caller] <i>Hello,</i>
<i>Miss Marten, this is Harry.</i>

900
00:48:10,375 --> 00:48:13,583
<i>I've got some wonderful news.</i>
<i>Are you as excited as I am?</i>

901
00:48:13,666 --> 00:48:14,791
Yes.

902
00:48:14,875 --> 00:48:17,333
<i>I am really pleased to tell</i>
<i>you that you've won a prize</i>

903
00:48:17,416 --> 00:48:19,208
<i>of £100,000,</i>

904
00:48:19,291 --> 00:48:21,291
<i>brought to you by Proton Economics.</i>

905
00:48:21,375 --> 00:48:23,583
<i>I can assure you, any personal details</i>

906
00:48:23,666 --> 00:48:26,541
<i>that you share with us</i>
<i>will be completely safe.</i>

907
00:48:26,625 --> 00:48:27,666
-[shrill whine]
<i>-We are a member</i>

908
00:48:27,750 --> 00:48:29,916
<i>of RCCP Online Security Forum.</i>

909
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:31,750
I know you're listening.

910
00:48:31,833 --> 00:48:32,916
<i>Of course I'm listening, ma'am.</i>

911
00:48:33,000 --> 00:48:34,000
No, not you.

912
00:48:34,833 --> 00:48:35,833
Him.

913
00:48:36,708 --> 00:48:38,458
[scam caller] <i>Sorry, who?</i>
<i>I don't understand.</i>

914
00:48:38,541 --> 00:48:39,916
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

915
00:48:40,000 --> 00:48:43,250
<i>I just need your bank details</i>
<i>and I can get it all sorted.</i>

916
00:48:43,333 --> 00:48:45,125
I can do this, do you hear me?

917
00:48:45,208 --> 00:48:46,791
[scam caller] <i>What?</i>

918
00:48:46,875 --> 00:48:48,375
[Maia] <i>Just give me a chance.</i>

919
00:48:48,458 --> 00:48:50,333
<i>This is your big chance, Miss Marten.</i>

920
00:48:50,416 --> 00:48:51,500
<i>-You're gonna be rich.</i>
-[ends call]

921
00:48:52,083 --> 00:48:54,125
-Hello?
-[caller breathes deeply]

922
00:48:54,208 --> 00:48:55,500
Hello?

923
00:48:55,583 --> 00:48:56,708
[caller breathes deeply]

924
00:48:56,791 --> 00:48:59,500
-Come on, come on, come on.
-[inhales deeply]

925
00:49:00,375 --> 00:49:02,625
-[caller exhales]
-Hello?

926
00:49:02,708 --> 00:49:03,750
It's over.

927
00:49:03,833 --> 00:49:05,041
No, no, no, no, no, no.

928
00:49:05,125 --> 00:49:07,291
I can still do this. I'll do anything.

929
00:49:07,375 --> 00:49:09,000
<i>-You broke the rules.</i>
-I had no choice.

930
00:49:09,083 --> 00:49:10,083
They stole my phone.

931
00:49:10,166 --> 00:49:11,708
[caller] You waved a gun around in public.

932
00:49:11,791 --> 00:49:14,291
And now the police
have a call out for you.

933
00:49:14,375 --> 00:49:15,458
You're useless to me now.

934
00:49:15,541 --> 00:49:17,666
I'm not useless. I can still do this.

935
00:49:18,541 --> 00:49:19,541
Please.

936
00:49:19,625 --> 00:49:22,375
[caller] No.
I'll have to handle it myself.

937
00:49:23,208 --> 00:49:25,416
<i>A lot of people are gonna die,</i>

938
00:49:25,500 --> 00:49:27,250
-not just Noah.
-[button clicks]

939
00:49:27,333 --> 00:49:29,166
-[beeping]
-It's gonna be messy

940
00:49:29,250 --> 00:49:30,458
<i>and that's your fault.</i>

941
00:49:31,666 --> 00:49:34,666
<i>I'm never wrong,</i>
<i>but I was wrong about you.</i>

942
00:49:37,458 --> 00:49:39,083
No, listen.

943
00:49:44,291 --> 00:49:46,083
[panting]

944
00:49:47,750 --> 00:49:49,541
You were only wrong about one thing.

945
00:49:52,291 --> 00:49:54,708
It wasn't my mother who killed my father,

946
00:49:56,166 --> 00:49:57,458
it was me.

947
00:50:01,166 --> 00:50:03,166
[Maia panting]

948
00:50:07,000 --> 00:50:08,375
Tell me.

949
00:50:12,583 --> 00:50:14,875
When my father was drunk,
he became an animal.

950
00:50:15,875 --> 00:50:17,750
[chuckles ruefully] The things he did…

951
00:50:19,250 --> 00:50:20,791
One night I came into the kitchen,

952
00:50:20,875 --> 00:50:22,833
and he was drinking milk from a carton.

953
00:50:27,125 --> 00:50:29,541
His fists were still wet with blood.

954
00:50:30,708 --> 00:50:32,333
<i>My mother's blood.</i>

955
00:50:34,541 --> 00:50:36,083
I aimed my target pistol at him

956
00:50:36,166 --> 00:50:37,500
and he wasn't even afraid.

957
00:50:39,541 --> 00:50:41,833
It's like he thought
nothing could hurt him.

958
00:50:46,916 --> 00:50:48,750
So he died surprised.

959
00:50:51,416 --> 00:50:54,250
I never told this to anyone. Only you.

960
00:50:56,708 --> 00:50:58,416
[sighs]

961
00:51:03,625 --> 00:51:05,125
Thank you.

962
00:51:08,166 --> 00:51:12,125
<i>So your mother went to jail</i>
<i>so you could have a life.</i>

963
00:51:14,625 --> 00:51:15,625
Yes.

964
00:51:15,708 --> 00:51:17,416
[Maia panting]

965
00:51:28,333 --> 00:51:30,166
Please give me another chance.

966
00:51:30,250 --> 00:51:32,125
[panting]

967
00:51:58,583 --> 00:52:00,041
<i>You have 15 minutes.</i>

968
00:52:00,750 --> 00:52:02,041
Thank you.

969
00:52:03,750 --> 00:52:05,833
[suspenseful music playing]

970
00:52:11,291 --> 00:52:13,458
[church bells toll]

971
00:52:18,208 --> 00:52:20,250
[beeping]

972
00:52:27,541 --> 00:52:29,208
[indistinct chatter]

973
00:52:29,291 --> 00:52:31,375
[brass band playing]

974
00:52:41,166 --> 00:52:43,166
[caller] <i>You should be able</i>
<i>to see the hotel now.</i>

975
00:52:44,958 --> 00:52:46,625
<i>You've got plenty of time.</i>

976
00:52:46,708 --> 00:52:48,625
[timer beeping]

977
00:52:53,166 --> 00:52:54,958
Shit. Police on the bridge.

978
00:52:59,333 --> 00:53:00,833
[caller] The whole area is crawling.

979
00:53:00,916 --> 00:53:02,791
You have to go to Blackfriars Bridge.

980
00:53:02,875 --> 00:53:04,291
[panting]

981
00:53:07,583 --> 00:53:08,916
I'll never make it.

982
00:53:18,916 --> 00:53:21,000
Just stop the drip.

983
00:53:21,083 --> 00:53:22,791
We're in this together now.

984
00:53:22,875 --> 00:53:24,750
[caller] Yes, we're a team now,

985
00:53:24,833 --> 00:53:26,458
<i>but remember what your father said.</i>

986
00:53:27,458 --> 00:53:31,208
Fear is a stronger
motivator than love. Hmm?

987
00:53:32,083 --> 00:53:33,583
<i>Police coming from</i>
<i>the other direction too.</i>

988
00:53:33,666 --> 00:53:35,875
<i>Take a hard left down the stairs.</i>

989
00:53:35,958 --> 00:53:38,125
[suspenseful music playing]

990
00:53:40,583 --> 00:53:42,166
[Maia panting]

991
00:53:47,458 --> 00:53:49,000
[map beeping]

992
00:53:50,083 --> 00:53:52,250
The police are on their way
to Blackfriars.

993
00:53:52,916 --> 00:53:54,500
<i>Gotta be quick, Maia.</i>

994
00:53:55,750 --> 00:53:57,541
[sirens wailing]

995
00:54:04,833 --> 00:54:07,625
-[officer] One Alpha Five.
-No, no, no.

996
00:54:07,708 --> 00:54:08,958
[caller] <i>Head to the underpass</i>
<i>to your left.</i>

997
00:54:17,583 --> 00:54:19,750
Waterloo is the only bridge
that's still open.

998
00:54:21,500 --> 00:54:23,708
If you keep this pace, you can do it.

999
00:54:23,791 --> 00:54:26,083
[Maia] It's half a mile
in the wrong direction.

1000
00:54:26,166 --> 00:54:27,208
I can't do that.

1001
00:54:27,291 --> 00:54:29,500
<i>-Use the fear, Maia.</i>
-Fuck you!

1002
00:54:33,333 --> 00:54:36,833
[Maia panting]

1003
00:54:42,500 --> 00:54:43,958
[groans]

1004
00:54:54,500 --> 00:54:56,041
<i>Police car coming towards you.</i>

1005
00:54:59,916 --> 00:55:01,541
[siren blaring]

1006
00:55:04,083 --> 00:55:05,833
[coughs]

1007
00:55:18,666 --> 00:55:21,791
[vendor] Hey, hey, hey! Stop, thief!

1008
00:55:21,875 --> 00:55:23,666
-Stop!
-[caller] <i>Up the steps.</i>

1009
00:55:23,750 --> 00:55:25,375
<i>Take a left.</i>

1010
00:55:37,416 --> 00:55:39,250
<i>Cross the street.</i>

1011
00:55:39,333 --> 00:55:41,416
<i>Take the alleyway behind King's College.</i>

1012
00:55:47,750 --> 00:55:49,791
Now go left on the Strand.

1013
00:55:57,291 --> 00:56:00,000
[timer beeping]

1014
00:56:06,833 --> 00:56:08,916
More police around the next corner.

1015
00:56:09,583 --> 00:56:12,125
There's a shortcut
that gets you onto the bridge.

1016
00:56:13,500 --> 00:56:15,958
<i>Take a left now through Somerset House.</i>

1017
00:56:16,041 --> 00:56:18,000
[suspenseful music playing]

1018
00:56:18,083 --> 00:56:19,958
[Maia panting]

1019
00:56:36,208 --> 00:56:38,208
[Maia panting]

1020
00:56:47,958 --> 00:56:50,416
[helicopter blades whirring]

1021
00:56:54,208 --> 00:56:55,333
[caller] There's a single policeman

1022
00:56:55,416 --> 00:56:56,708
coming towards you.

1023
00:56:57,625 --> 00:56:59,083
Blend into the crowd.

1024
00:57:02,541 --> 00:57:03,666
<i>Twenty metres.</i>

1025
00:57:07,291 --> 00:57:08,583
<i>Fifteen metres.</i>

1026
00:57:11,333 --> 00:57:13,083
<i>Ten metres.</i>

1027
00:57:16,750 --> 00:57:18,041
<i>Five metres.</i>

1028
00:57:18,125 --> 00:57:20,041
[passers-by chatting indistinctly]

1029
00:57:20,125 --> 00:57:22,375
[woman] My God, he was so cute!

1030
00:57:22,458 --> 00:57:25,166
-[women whooping, laughing]
-[woman] Sorry, sorry.

1031
00:57:26,500 --> 00:57:28,416
-[officer] Control, suspect…
-No, no, no.

1032
00:57:28,500 --> 00:57:30,583
-[people clamouring]
-[woman] She's got a gun!

1033
00:57:30,666 --> 00:57:31,958
[man] Come on, go!

1034
00:57:32,041 --> 00:57:33,875
[dispatcher] <i>…believed to be</i>
<i>armed with a black handgun…</i>

1035
00:57:33,958 --> 00:57:35,000
Take your hand off that!

1036
00:57:35,083 --> 00:57:37,208
[dispatcher] <i>Suspect is Maia Marten.</i>

1037
00:57:37,291 --> 00:57:39,625
Take it easy. Take it easy.

1038
00:57:39,708 --> 00:57:41,916
-[caller] <i>Take his radio.</i>
-I don't need your help.

1039
00:57:42,833 --> 00:57:45,083
-[officer] Please, ma'am.
-Get back! Get back!

1040
00:57:45,166 --> 00:57:47,041
-Get back!
-[crowd clamours, screams]

1041
00:57:47,125 --> 00:57:48,958
[officer] Please, drop the weapon.

1042
00:57:49,041 --> 00:57:52,000
Give me your radio. On your knees now!

1043
00:57:52,083 --> 00:57:54,375
I said, give me the radio.

1044
00:57:54,458 --> 00:57:55,875
-[sirens wailing]
-[gunshot]

1045
00:57:55,958 --> 00:57:57,750
[crowd screaming]

1046
00:58:00,250 --> 00:58:02,583
[caller] Multiple police cars
incoming, Maia.

1047
00:58:02,666 --> 00:58:04,166
Armed units.

1048
00:58:07,000 --> 00:58:08,625
[tyres squealing]

1049
00:58:08,708 --> 00:58:10,083
<i>-You're trapped!</i>
-[officer 1] Armed police!

1050
00:58:10,166 --> 00:58:11,375
[officer 2] Armed police!

1051
00:58:11,458 --> 00:58:13,666
-[officer 3] Police, drop the weapon!
-[caller] <i>It's over!</i>

1052
00:58:13,750 --> 00:58:15,708
[police shout orders indistinctly]

1053
00:58:15,791 --> 00:58:18,291
[Maia panting]

1054
00:58:18,375 --> 00:58:20,583
[officer] Failure to comply,
we will use lethal force!

1055
00:58:22,250 --> 00:58:24,458
[caller] <i>I'm sorry that Noah's</i>
<i>gonna die without you.</i>

1056
00:58:25,416 --> 00:58:27,250
No, that's not gonna happen.

1057
00:58:28,458 --> 00:58:30,041
Ma'am. Let me help you.

1058
00:58:30,125 --> 00:58:32,166
Shut the fuck up!

1059
00:58:32,958 --> 00:58:34,458
[officer 1] Whatever trouble you're in,

1060
00:58:34,541 --> 00:58:35,541
we can still fix it.

1061
00:58:35,625 --> 00:58:37,916
[officer 2] Drop the weapon!
Put the gun down!

1062
00:58:38,000 --> 00:58:39,041
[caller] <i>What are you doing?</i>

1063
00:58:39,125 --> 00:58:41,083
I thought you knew everything.

1064
00:58:41,833 --> 00:58:43,458
[crowd gasps and screams]

1065
00:58:46,708 --> 00:58:48,125
[clamouring]

1066
00:58:49,583 --> 00:58:52,000
Maia? Maia?

1067
00:58:52,083 --> 00:58:53,500
[mouse clicking]

1068
00:58:53,583 --> 00:58:55,958
[clamouring]

1069
00:58:58,541 --> 00:59:01,416
-Maia!
-[beeping]

1070
00:59:03,041 --> 00:59:05,541
[indistinct overlapping chatter]

1071
00:59:10,083 --> 00:59:12,375
-[caller] Jesus.
-[woman] <i>Oh, my God!</i>

1072
00:59:12,458 --> 00:59:15,833
-[woman] <i>Holy shit!</i>
-[laughs] Maia!

1073
00:59:20,083 --> 00:59:21,083
[Noah] <i>Mummy!</i>

1074
00:59:21,166 --> 00:59:23,541
["Delilah" playing]

1075
00:59:26,750 --> 00:59:27,833
<i>Are you here?</i>

1076
00:59:27,916 --> 00:59:30,375
[song continues muffled]

1077
00:59:34,166 --> 00:59:35,375
[Maia exhales]

1078
00:59:35,458 --> 00:59:37,541
[boatman] What the hell
are you doing up here?

1079
00:59:43,250 --> 00:59:46,833
I need you to take me
to London Bridge, south side.

1080
00:59:46,916 --> 00:59:48,250
[panting]

1081
00:59:51,041 --> 00:59:52,750
But if you don't get me there
in six minutes,

1082
00:59:52,833 --> 00:59:54,541
my son will be dead.

1083
00:59:57,500 --> 01:00:01,958
[woman]
♪ <i>My, my, my, Delilah </i>♪

1084
01:00:05,083 --> 01:00:09,708
♪ <i>Why, why, why, Delilah? ♪</i>

1085
01:00:12,541 --> 01:00:14,500
♪ <i>So before ♪</i>

1086
01:00:14,583 --> 01:00:15,916
[inaudible]

1087
01:00:16,000 --> 01:00:18,583
♪ <i>They come</i>
<i>To break down the door ♪</i>

1088
01:00:18,666 --> 01:00:19,833
I'll take her.

1089
01:00:19,916 --> 01:00:21,458
♪ <i>Forgive me, Delilah ♪</i>

1090
01:00:21,541 --> 01:00:24,208
♪ <i>I just couldn't take</i>
<i>Any more ♪</i>

1091
01:00:24,291 --> 01:00:26,041
[TV reporter] <i>As you can see,</i>
<i>security is already heavy</i>

1092
01:00:26,125 --> 01:00:28,041
<i>here at the Old Bailey</i>

1093
01:00:28,125 --> 01:00:31,041
<i>as the legal teams begin to arrive</i>
<i>for Tommy Boyd's murder trial.</i>

1094
01:00:31,125 --> 01:00:32,875
<i>Tantalisingly, we're hearing reports</i>

1095
01:00:32,958 --> 01:00:36,125
<i>of a surprise witness</i>
<i>inside Mr Boyd's organisation,</i>

1096
01:00:36,208 --> 01:00:38,291
<i>whose testimony is said to be devastating</i>

1097
01:00:38,375 --> 01:00:40,083
<i>for the alleged criminal kingpin.</i>

1098
01:00:40,166 --> 01:00:42,333
<i>Back to you, Mike, for the weather.</i>

1099
01:00:42,416 --> 01:00:43,750
See the <i>HMS Belfast </i>up ahead?

1100
01:00:45,208 --> 01:00:47,666
I can get us near enough
for you to jump onto the jetty

1101
01:00:47,750 --> 01:00:49,125
but I can't stop.

1102
01:00:50,666 --> 01:00:52,250
Can you do that?

1103
01:00:53,625 --> 01:00:56,041
-Take the starboard door.
-Thank you.

1104
01:00:57,666 --> 01:01:01,250
I broke your special rules,
your stupid freaking rules.

1105
01:01:01,333 --> 01:01:03,125
[caller] <i>Rules are made to be broken.</i>

1106
01:01:03,958 --> 01:01:06,208
<i>This is the end game.</i>

1107
01:01:13,500 --> 01:01:15,208
[indistinct chatter]

1108
01:01:19,000 --> 01:01:20,041
[Maia grunts]

1109
01:01:26,500 --> 01:01:28,750
[man] …Belfast, beautiful day for it.

1110
01:01:28,833 --> 01:01:31,125
-It's a pride…
-[Maia grunts]

1111
01:01:33,625 --> 01:01:35,083
[suspenseful music playing]

1112
01:01:38,958 --> 01:01:40,250
[panting]

1113
01:01:43,750 --> 01:01:45,166
[timer beeping]

1114
01:02:06,375 --> 01:02:09,333
[Maia] They're here, the security detail,

1115
01:02:09,416 --> 01:02:11,083
getting ready to move him.

1116
01:02:11,166 --> 01:02:13,458
[caller] <i>No time to waste, then.</i>

1117
01:02:13,541 --> 01:02:15,250
<i>Noah's breathing is getting shallow.</i>

1118
01:02:26,625 --> 01:02:27,708
I got this. Okay.

1119
01:02:27,791 --> 01:02:29,041
[music fades]

1120
01:02:34,375 --> 01:02:36,875
["The Entertainer" playing]

1121
01:02:36,958 --> 01:02:38,583
[breathing heavily]

1122
01:02:50,625 --> 01:02:52,291
You're here, aren't you?

1123
01:02:52,375 --> 01:02:54,208
-["The Entertainer" distorts]
-[eerie music plays]

1124
01:02:57,291 --> 01:03:00,458
[caller] <i>There are 267 rooms</i>
<i>in this establishment.</i>

1125
01:03:03,958 --> 01:03:06,541
<i>Could you find a Noah in the haystack?</i>

1126
01:03:08,541 --> 01:03:11,541
<i>Do your job, then you'll get</i>
<i>the room number.</i>

1127
01:03:12,208 --> 01:03:15,875
Er, excuse me, madam,
may I ask where you're going?

1128
01:03:16,916 --> 01:03:20,125
I'm visiting a client,
Imperial Suite, 53rd floor.

1129
01:03:23,416 --> 01:03:24,541
Just one moment, please.

1130
01:03:24,625 --> 01:03:25,625
No, no, no, no.

1131
01:03:26,833 --> 01:03:29,333
Listen, listen, listen, sir,
I don't have time for this.

1132
01:03:29,416 --> 01:03:31,291
-I have a Ms…
-I don't have time for this.

1133
01:03:31,375 --> 01:03:32,375
I need to go upstairs, please.

1134
01:03:32,458 --> 01:03:33,500
-What's your name, please?
-Maia Marten.

1135
01:03:33,583 --> 01:03:35,750
-It's an emergency.
-Maia Marten.

1136
01:03:41,041 --> 01:03:42,333
-Yes, okay.
-Sir.

1137
01:03:42,416 --> 01:03:43,416
That's fine.

1138
01:03:45,041 --> 01:03:46,500
You can go up now, Ms Marten.

1139
01:03:47,541 --> 01:03:49,083
-Have a good day, madam.
-[timer beeping]

1140
01:03:50,625 --> 01:03:52,166
[lift bell dings]

1141
01:03:54,208 --> 01:03:55,958
-[caller] <i>Check the gun.</i>
-[pouch unzips]

1142
01:03:57,375 --> 01:03:59,083
-[cartridge clatters]
-[panting]

1143
01:04:02,583 --> 01:04:04,375
<i>Open your phone so I can see you.</i>

1144
01:04:09,375 --> 01:04:11,458
<i>A little reminder of what's at stake.</i>

1145
01:04:11,541 --> 01:04:13,333
[stifles sob]

1146
01:04:17,000 --> 01:04:19,333
Now put it back on your arm,
facing forward.

1147
01:04:22,000 --> 01:04:24,583
<i>I need to see you do this</i>
<i>with my own eyes.</i>

1148
01:04:24,666 --> 01:04:26,125
[Maia breathing deeply]

1149
01:04:26,208 --> 01:04:28,083
[timer beeping]

1150
01:04:28,166 --> 01:04:29,833
[suspenseful music playing]

1151
01:04:43,416 --> 01:04:44,791
[lift bell dings]

1152
01:04:47,875 --> 01:04:49,250
-[liquid drips]
-[timer clicks]

1153
01:05:03,833 --> 01:05:04,958
-[liquid drips]
-[timer clicks]

1154
01:05:06,958 --> 01:05:08,750
-Morning.
-[guard] Good morning, ma'am.

1155
01:05:08,833 --> 01:05:11,500
I need to have a last-minute
chat with my client.

1156
01:05:11,583 --> 01:05:13,833
Been for a run, ma'am?

1157
01:05:13,916 --> 01:05:15,458
Have I ever.

1158
01:05:17,458 --> 01:05:19,416
You should get that cut seen to, ma'am.

1159
01:05:19,500 --> 01:05:21,000
[commentator] <i>It was a really</i>
<i>difficult chance,</i>

1160
01:05:21,083 --> 01:05:22,708
<i>diving forward.</i>

1161
01:05:23,666 --> 01:05:25,875
<i>He just couldn't quite get</i>
<i>his fingers under the ball.</i>

1162
01:05:26,416 --> 01:05:28,791
<i>He did well to stop it, to be fair.</i>

1163
01:05:34,541 --> 01:05:36,041
[timer clicks]

1164
01:05:43,333 --> 01:05:45,500
-[knocks]
-[Tafa] Come in.

1165
01:05:46,750 --> 01:05:48,416
Hello, Maia.

1166
01:05:48,500 --> 01:05:50,500
-[locks door]
-Do you like my new suit?

1167
01:05:51,333 --> 01:05:53,166
I got it for the big day.

1168
01:05:55,666 --> 01:05:57,125
You look like shit.

1169
01:05:59,625 --> 01:06:00,916
Maia?

1170
01:06:01,000 --> 01:06:02,500
Wait, wait. What you doing?

1171
01:06:03,250 --> 01:06:04,708
-[gunshot]
-[Tafa yells]

1172
01:06:04,791 --> 01:06:06,500
[gunshots]

1173
01:06:07,583 --> 01:06:08,791
[Tafa groans]

1174
01:06:08,875 --> 01:06:11,000
[Maia panting]

1175
01:06:16,625 --> 01:06:19,291
[guard] What's going on?
Ma'am, open the door!

1176
01:06:19,375 --> 01:06:21,166
{\an8}-[knocking at door]
-[message alerts ping]

1177
01:06:21,250 --> 01:06:23,416
{\an8}[guard shouting indistinctly]

1178
01:06:35,541 --> 01:06:38,541
[door opens, closes]

1179
01:06:38,625 --> 01:06:40,458
[alarm blaring]

1180
01:06:55,166 --> 01:06:57,416
[overlapping chatter]

1181
01:06:58,750 --> 01:06:59,750
[people clamouring]

1182
01:06:59,833 --> 01:07:00,875
[Maia] Let me through! Out of my way!

1183
01:07:00,958 --> 01:07:02,791
-Let me through!
-[woman gasps]

1184
01:07:02,875 --> 01:07:04,041
[man] Come on, darling, let's go!

1185
01:07:05,458 --> 01:07:06,916
-Come on.
-Out of my way! Out of my way!

1186
01:07:07,000 --> 01:07:08,708
[people clamouring]

1187
01:07:11,125 --> 01:07:12,541
-[alarm blaring]
-[Maia panting]

1188
01:07:23,625 --> 01:07:24,791
[grunts]

1189
01:07:32,791 --> 01:07:34,791
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

1190
01:07:34,875 --> 01:07:37,083
Okay, Noah, wake up!

1191
01:07:37,166 --> 01:07:38,791
Mummy's here. Wake up.

1192
01:07:39,958 --> 01:07:42,208
Noah, wake up! [breathing heavily]

1193
01:07:50,750 --> 01:07:53,000
Noah. Noah.

1194
01:07:54,041 --> 01:07:56,500
Noah! Come on. Wake up.

1195
01:07:56,583 --> 01:07:58,500
Noah, come on! [grunts]

1196
01:08:00,541 --> 01:08:03,541
Noah, monkey, please don't leave me.

1197
01:08:03,625 --> 01:08:05,041
Come back!

1198
01:08:08,833 --> 01:08:10,000
[sobs]

1199
